WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

2
00:02:13.216 --> 00:02:14.217
(MAN SPEAKING SPANISH)

3
00:02:14.384 --> 00:02:16.845
We swap in parts from Fords...

4
00:02:17.053 --> 00:02:18.680
...Plymouths and Cadillacs.

5
00:02:19.431 --> 00:02:21.349
My grandfather bought it in 1957.

6
00:02:21.683 --> 00:02:23.143
When he died. it passed to my father.

7
00:02:23.351 --> 00:02:24.811
Then my brother. and now to me.

8
00:02:24.894 --> 00:02:25.895
Look at this.

9
00:02:26.229 --> 00:02:27.814
This is an engine from a boat.

10
00:02:27.897 --> 00:02:29.482
- (IN ENGLISH) No way!
- MAN: Yeah. (CONTINUING IN SPANISH)

11
00:02:29.566 --> 00:02:31.526
Whatever it takes to keep it running.

12
00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:33.862
(IN ENGLISH) This is the Cuban spirit.
(CONTINUING IN SPANISH)

13
00:02:33.945 --> 00:02:35.321
Your spirit.

14
00:02:35.447 --> 00:02:36.493
Don't ever lose that.

15
00:02:36.573 --> 00:02:37.615
Dom. Dom. (IN SPANISH)

16
00:02:37.741 --> 00:02:38.783
It's your cousin.

17
00:02:38.867 --> 00:02:40.910
He's in trouble.

18
00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.537
Come on!

19
00:02:43.413 --> 00:02:44.414
(ENGINE REVVING)

20
00:02:44.581 --> 00:02:45.582
(ALL CHEERING)

21
00:02:51.212 --> 00:02:54.052
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

22
00:02:54.132 --> 00:02:56.009
(IN ENGLISH) You know I can't
make a living without my car.

23
00:02:56.092 --> 00:02:57.594
Not my problem. bro.

24
00:02:58.595 --> 00:03:02.265
Dominic Toretto. I heard about you.
Welcome to my island.

25
00:03:02.557 --> 00:03:03.933
Why you hookin' up my cousin's car?

26
00:03:04.642 --> 00:03:06.436
He needed money. I gave it to him.

27
00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:08.646
He can't pay. I take the car.

28
00:03:08.772 --> 00:03:09.814
I just need a few more days.

29
00:03:09.939 --> 00:03:11.399
"Few more days" wasn't part of the deal.

30
00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:15.407
Come on. You make a deal.
you gotta live up to it.

31
00:03:15.487 --> 00:03:18.073
You make a deal. you gonna live up to it.

32
00:03:18.948 --> 00:03:20.408
"Gonna" live up to it?

33
00:03:22.619 --> 00:03:24.162
Oh. so you're one of those types.

34
00:03:24.829 --> 00:03:26.790
You take everyone's ride.
and then ship it back to the States?

35
00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:27.874
(IN SPANISH)

36
00:03:27.957 --> 00:03:30.001
You should show your people some respect.

37
00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:31.461
(IN ENGLISH) You watch your mouth.

38
00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:32.754
(CHUCKLES)

39
00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.131
Now you got a problem.

40
00:03:38.468 --> 00:03:40.220
- I'm gonna keep it about the cars.
- (IN SPANISH)

41
00:03:40.303 --> 00:03:43.181
I'm really scared.

42
00:03:43.306 --> 00:03:44.641
(IN ENGLISH)
You want a car. get it the right way.

43
00:03:45.183 --> 00:03:46.226
How?

44
00:03:46.768 --> 00:03:47.977
Race for it.

45
00:03:48.311 --> 00:03:50.146
I already own it. bro.

46
00:03:51.022 --> 00:03:52.482
Not that car.

47
00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:55.068
Mine.

48
00:03:55.151 --> 00:03:56.152
(CROWD EXCLAIMING)

49
00:03:56.486 --> 00:03:59.280
Dom. his car is
the fastest car on the island.

50
00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.032
Do you know what he has under that hood?

51
00:04:01.324 --> 00:04:03.493
He knows it doesn't matter
what's under a hood.

52
00:04:04.369 --> 00:04:07.372
The only thing that matters
is who's behind the wheel.

53
00:04:07.455 --> 00:04:08.498
You think so?

54
00:04:08.832 --> 00:04:10.000
I know so.

55
00:04:10.375 --> 00:04:12.043
Then race his car.

56
00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:16.589
And we ain't racing no quarter-mile. here.

57
00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:18.508
We race the Cuban mile.

58
00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:21.219
Done.

59
00:04:21.302 --> 00:04:23.346
(CROWD CHEERING)

60
00:04:25.473 --> 00:04:26.725
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

61
00:04:36.151 --> 00:04:40.613
I appreciate what you're trying to do.
but my car is the slowest car on the island.

62
00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:44.868
Was.

63
00:04:45.744 --> 00:04:47.787
Pull the seats. the doors. the battery...

64
00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:50.415
If it ain't the motor. take it off.

65
00:04:51.332 --> 00:04:52.417
Laughing gas?

66
00:04:52.751 --> 00:04:54.753
Nah. Fed. This is Cuban NOS.

67
00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:56.713
You guys are crazy.

68
00:04:58.715 --> 00:04:59.883
What are you doing?

69
00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:03.553
DOM: Poor man's turbo.
Pull the vacuum line and hold on.

70
00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:06.890
Old trick that Buster used to play.
in case of emergencies.

71
00:05:07.557 --> 00:05:09.893
You know that's way too much
boost for that engine.

72
00:05:10.226 --> 00:05:11.227
DOM: It's gonna be fast.

73
00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:12.687
It's gonna be a bomb.

74
00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.565
Only needs to go a mile.

75
00:05:20.737 --> 00:05:22.655
(CROWD CHEERING)

76
00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:27.243
(ENGINES REVVING)

77
00:05:41.257 --> 00:05:42.220
(IN SPANISH)

78
00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:44.344
Are you ready for this. my family?

79
00:05:44.594 --> 00:05:46.721
This is Havana!

80
00:05:48.431 --> 00:05:50.558
Be fast.

81
00:05:51.142 --> 00:05:53.269
Be safe.

82
00:05:53.561 --> 00:05:56.856
But don't be last. Racers ready!

83
00:05:57.565 --> 00:05:58.817
<i>Vamonos!</i>

84
00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:27.971
(TIRES SQUEALING)

85
00:06:31.641 --> 00:06:32.642
(LAUGHING)

86
00:06:36.646 --> 00:06:38.982
(IN ENGLISH)
That car belongs in the trash. bro!

87
00:06:54.289 --> 00:06:55.331
(TIRES SQUEALING)

88
00:06:55.457 --> 00:06:56.499
(HORN BLARING)

89
00:07:11.181 --> 00:07:12.223
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

90
00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:15.685
(CHILDREN CHEERING)

91
00:07:28.698 --> 00:07:30.950
- FERNANDO: Where are they going?
- LETTY: I don't know. Let's go!

92
00:07:45.048 --> 00:07:46.049
(CELL PHONE BEEPS)

93
00:07:46.132 --> 00:07:47.133
Ghost him.

94
00:07:47.384 --> 00:07:48.385
MAN: <i>Sí.</i>

95
00:07:48.468 --> 00:07:49.469
(PEOPLE YELLING)

96
00:08:06.945 --> 00:08:08.738
<i>Adiós.</i> Toretto!

97
00:08:12.742 --> 00:08:14.077
Okay. Buster.

98
00:08:14.744 --> 00:08:16.246
Let's see if this works.

99
00:08:17.997 --> 00:08:19.708
- (TIRES SQUEALING)
- (ENGINE REVVING)

100
00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:25.380
That's impossible.

101
00:08:57.454 --> 00:08:59.414
(ALL CHEERING)

102
00:09:04.127 --> 00:09:05.128
(GLASS SHATTERING)

103
00:09:07.422 --> 00:09:08.965
(TIRES SQUEAL)

104
00:09:25.899 --> 00:09:27.359
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

105
00:09:36.868 --> 00:09:38.078
(EXCLAIMS)

106
00:09:41.039 --> 00:09:42.415
(CHEERING)

107
00:09:44.584 --> 00:09:45.627
(IN ENGLISH) Look out!

108
00:10:01.935 --> 00:10:03.895
(ALL CONTINUE CHEERING)

109
00:10:40.765 --> 00:10:41.850
A deal's a deal.

110
00:10:43.518 --> 00:10:44.686
You won my car.

111
00:10:46.855 --> 00:10:48.481
And you earned my respect.

112
00:11:03.329 --> 00:11:04.664
Keep your car.

113
00:11:05.749 --> 00:11:07.500
Your respect is good enough for me.

114
00:11:12.964 --> 00:11:14.215
DOM: Yo. cousin...

115
00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:16.926
Sorry about your car.

116
00:11:22.015 --> 00:11:24.517
Yours was too slow for a Toretto. anyway.

117
00:11:24.601 --> 00:11:27.270
Your Impala? Are you serious?

118
00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:30.440
(ALL CHEERING)

119
00:12:14.317 --> 00:12:15.860
Look at that smile.

120
00:12:16.403 --> 00:12:18.029
I love it when you smile.

121
00:12:18.113 --> 00:12:19.406
You make me happy.

122
00:12:20.198 --> 00:12:22.742
Mmm. I think this place makes you happy.

123
00:12:25.161 --> 00:12:26.579
It's like it speaks to you.

124
00:12:30.166 --> 00:12:33.461
You remember that guy. the racer and his dad?

125
00:12:34.504 --> 00:12:35.759
The one with the boat engine under the hood?

126
00:12:35.839 --> 00:12:36.840
Yeah!

127
00:12:36.965 --> 00:12:38.595
- Yes.
- Of course.

128
00:12:38.675 --> 00:12:41.636
I was looking at them. and I...

129
00:12:42.178 --> 00:12:46.349
And I couldn't help but to imagine
what you'd be like if you were a dad.

130
00:12:48.685 --> 00:12:51.021
No. no. no! I'm not pregnant.

131
00:12:55.150 --> 00:12:56.234
Is that what you want?

132
00:12:57.318 --> 00:12:59.696
It's not about what I want or what you want.

133
00:13:00.488 --> 00:13:03.116
It's about why we haven't asked the question.

134
00:13:20.842 --> 00:13:22.469
(ENGINE CRANKS SLOWLY)

135
00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:28.266
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

136
00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:31.811
- (IN ENGLISH) What?
- You need a hand?

137
00:13:33.063 --> 00:13:34.314
Yeah. I think I do.

138
00:13:35.106 --> 00:13:37.400
- Sounds like you're not getting any fuel.
- Yeah?

139
00:13:37.484 --> 00:13:39.402
Probably the shut-off solenoid.

140
00:13:39.819 --> 00:13:41.279
Let's see if we can get some power to it.

141
00:13:43.907 --> 00:13:45.408
What brings you to Cuba?

142
00:13:47.202 --> 00:13:49.245
The same thing that brings
everyone else to Cuba.

143
00:13:50.288 --> 00:13:52.749
Culture. people. the beauty.

144
00:13:53.458 --> 00:13:54.834
What brings you to Cuba?

145
00:13:55.377 --> 00:13:57.712
- Work.
- Must be casual Friday.

146
00:13:59.547 --> 00:14:00.965
How's that honeymoon going. Dom?

147
00:14:06.805 --> 00:14:08.765
Your fuel relay is missing.

148
00:14:10.892 --> 00:14:12.143
I know.

149
00:14:15.772 --> 00:14:17.402
I love to play games.

150
00:14:17.482 --> 00:14:19.067
I've beaten the best of 'em.

151
00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:22.487
But I'm kind of in a rush.
so if you've got something to say to me...

152
00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:24.948
Oh. this is a very different game.
that I can assure you.

153
00:14:25.990 --> 00:14:30.286
This... There's something
much greater at work here.

154
00:14:31.079 --> 00:14:32.080
This is fate.

155
00:14:32.789 --> 00:14:34.416
I choose to make my own fate.

156
00:14:34.624 --> 00:14:36.042
Not today.

157
00:14:36.668 --> 00:14:39.671
Is this the road you take
to your apartment every morning?

158
00:14:39.838 --> 00:14:42.841
What else is different. Dom?
Was Santiago's closed?

159
00:14:43.008 --> 00:14:45.135
Did you have to cross two blocks
to go get your Cuban coffees?

160
00:14:45.218 --> 00:14:47.470
What is it. black. no sugar?

161
00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:49.973
Yeah.

162
00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:52.475
I put a lot of work into
getting you here today.

163
00:14:53.351 --> 00:14:54.978
Well. now that I'm here. what do you want?

164
00:14:55.437 --> 00:14:56.688
I want you to work for me.

165
00:14:58.356 --> 00:14:59.357
Work for you?

166
00:14:59.858 --> 00:15:02.027
Oh. I could've saved you a lot of time. then.

167
00:15:02.485 --> 00:15:03.903
See. I don't work for anyone.

168
00:15:04.487 --> 00:15:06.409
You can't walk away from this. Dom.

169
00:15:06.489 --> 00:15:08.992
We're gonna have this conversation.
one way or the other.

170
00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:12.203
You see. that's the funny thing about fate.

171
00:15:13.121 --> 00:15:14.289
It's cunning.

172
00:15:14.873 --> 00:15:18.501
It can bring you beautiful things.
and it can also bring you moments like this.

173
00:15:32.390 --> 00:15:34.809
Oh. you're gonna want to work for me.

174
00:15:35.393 --> 00:15:39.609
You're gonna betray your brothers.
abandon your code. and shatter your family.

175
00:15:39.689 --> 00:15:44.194
You see. your team is about to go up
against the only thing they can't handle.

176
00:15:45.195 --> 00:15:46.196
What's that?

177
00:15:48.198 --> 00:15:49.532
You.

178
00:15:50.992 --> 00:15:53.787
Oh. and. Dom.
I wouldn't mention this to anyone.

179
00:15:56.456 --> 00:15:57.749
(ENGINE STARTS)

180
00:16:03.213 --> 00:16:06.383
HOBBS: <i>They are gonna be hitting us
with everything they got.</i>

181
00:16:06.675 --> 00:16:08.680
So we wanna engage with maximum speed.

182
00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:12.180
Neutralize their shooters.
and then move on to our objective.

183
00:16:12.347 --> 00:16:14.391
There's two things
I want you to keep in mind.

184
00:16:14.557 --> 00:16:16.980
Number one. I chose you for this squad

185
00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:20.939
because you are the most
fearsome warriors on the planet.

186
00:16:21.022 --> 00:16:23.028
And number two. you go out there.

187
00:16:23.108 --> 00:16:25.864
you do your job. and you take 'em down.

188
00:16:25.944 --> 00:16:28.196
Everyone. And I mean everyone.

189
00:16:28.947 --> 00:16:31.825
Mani's and pedi's at the mall later on today.

190
00:16:32.117 --> 00:16:33.660
(ALL CHEERING)

191
00:16:34.119 --> 00:16:35.161
Huh?

192
00:16:36.454 --> 00:16:37.956
- (WHISTLE BLOWING)
- GIRLS: Monarchs!

193
00:16:39.874 --> 00:16:42.043
(CHANTING HAKA)

194
00:17:01.187 --> 00:17:03.606
(ALL CHANTING HAKA)

195
00:17:19.289 --> 00:17:20.623
(EXCLAIMS)

196
00:17:23.126 --> 00:17:24.252
(EXHALES SHARPLY)

197
00:17:26.254 --> 00:17:27.255
(WHISPERS) What?

198
00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:28.381
(WHISTLE BLOWS)

199
00:17:31.301 --> 00:17:32.635
I don't wanna play anymore.

200
00:17:34.471 --> 00:17:36.139
All right. let's go. girls.
Let's go. let's go!

201
00:17:36.306 --> 00:17:37.307
Final two minutes.

202
00:17:37.474 --> 00:17:38.475
DS ALLAN: Quite the cheering section.

203
00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:43.021
HOBBS: Oh. yeah.

204
00:17:43.480 --> 00:17:45.648
Yeah. it's the moms.
They come out to support the kids.

205
00:17:45.815 --> 00:17:48.109
Except there seem to be more moms than kids.

206
00:17:48.526 --> 00:17:49.652
Way more moms.

207
00:17:51.154 --> 00:17:52.405
(WOMEN GIGGLING)

208
00:17:52.489 --> 00:17:54.783
(CHUCKLES) Yeah. It's a big soccer town.

209
00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:56.326
Let's go. girls!

210
00:17:56.618 --> 00:17:58.244
So. your intel was spot-on.

211
00:17:58.453 --> 00:18:00.830
That Damocles 7 EMP weapon
that went missing in the Gulf?

212
00:18:01.122 --> 00:18:03.792
Arms dealers from the Liberation
Front have it in Berlin.

213
00:18:03.875 --> 00:18:04.918
HOBBS: Shit!

214
00:18:05.001 --> 00:18:07.757
This thing can wipe out
an entire electrical grid in a major city.

215
00:18:07.837 --> 00:18:09.297
No lights. no power.

216
00:18:09.464 --> 00:18:10.465
Instant Stone Age.

217
00:18:10.590 --> 00:18:12.884
Chloe. Maya.
you can't let her run by you like that.

218
00:18:12.967 --> 00:18:16.096
- Let's go. let's go! Cross!
- Agent Hobbs. this is a Class Four WMD.

219
00:18:16.179 --> 00:18:17.514
Do you have any idea what's at stake here?

220
00:18:17.597 --> 00:18:20.266
Yes. I know exactly
what is at stake here. okay?

221
00:18:20.350 --> 00:18:23.978
If the Pink Butterflies beat my Red Dragons.
that means we lose the championship.

222
00:18:25.146 --> 00:18:28.278
Which means I have 20 little girls who
are crying. and that's not a good thing.

223
00:18:28.358 --> 00:18:31.156
Which then means I have to spend
a lot of time in ice-cream shops

224
00:18:31.236 --> 00:18:32.987
and a lot of time at Tay Tay concerts.

225
00:18:33.530 --> 00:18:34.572
Tay Tay?

226
00:18:35.657 --> 00:18:39.077
Taylor Swift. Gotta be shittin' me.
Get it together. okay?

227
00:18:39.244 --> 00:18:40.245
Let's go. girls!

228
00:18:40.412 --> 00:18:42.706
We need you to do this.
It's a lot of lives at stake.

229
00:18:42.872 --> 00:18:44.416
All right. but I need to be clear here.

230
00:18:44.749 --> 00:18:47.460
The US government cannot sanction
this operation in any way.

231
00:18:47.711 --> 00:18:48.878
- You're on your own.
- Hey.

232
00:18:49.045 --> 00:18:51.464
If this thing goes sideways.
you don't just get burned.

233
00:18:51.631 --> 00:18:52.841
You go to prison.

234
00:18:53.425 --> 00:18:55.343
And there's nothing we can do to get you out.

235
00:18:56.553 --> 00:18:57.595
Let me tell you something.

236
00:18:58.138 --> 00:19:03.143
The only thing that I love more
than saving lives is my daughter.

237
00:19:03.309 --> 00:19:06.104
So. if you don't shut up
with this government bullshit right now.

238
00:19:06.271 --> 00:19:10.984
and start showing some team spirit
and respect for the Red Dragons.

239
00:19:11.443 --> 00:19:14.821
I'm gonna have all 20 of them line up
and kick you right in the tay-tay.

240
00:19:17.949 --> 00:19:19.117
Go Dragons!

241
00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:21.244
Say it again.

242
00:19:21.411 --> 00:19:22.620
Go Dragons!

243
00:19:22.787 --> 00:19:24.748
Attaboy. Go Dragons.

244
00:19:25.081 --> 00:19:26.291
- Go Dragons.
- (CROWD EXCLAIMS)

245
00:19:26.458 --> 00:19:28.752
- SAM: I'm open.
- She's open! Go. go!

246
00:19:29.044 --> 00:19:30.170
Yes! (LAUGHING)

247
00:19:30.295 --> 00:19:31.463
(WHISTLE BLOWS)

248
00:19:31.671 --> 00:19:33.590
That is my daughter right there. Yes.

249
00:19:34.507 --> 00:19:35.845
Yes. come here.

250
00:19:35.925 --> 00:19:36.926
How did I do?

251
00:19:37.260 --> 00:19:38.261
Awesome.

252
00:19:38.345 --> 00:19:39.346
Nice job. kid.

253
00:19:43.058 --> 00:19:44.726
- (HOBBS SIGHS)
- Daddy's gotta go to work?

254
00:19:45.018 --> 00:19:47.312
Uh. yeah. Daddy's gotta go to work.

255
00:19:48.063 --> 00:19:49.898
Now. you're gonna need
to get a team you can trust.

256
00:19:50.815 --> 00:19:52.108
Oh. I already got one.

257
00:19:58.698 --> 00:20:00.241
(CELL PHONE VIBRATING)

258
00:20:10.126 --> 00:20:11.336
(SIGHS)

259
00:20:13.380 --> 00:20:14.381
HOBBS: <i>Hey. Dom.</i>

260
00:20:14.714 --> 00:20:15.715
Hey. Hobbs.

261
00:20:15.882 --> 00:20:17.967
<i>I got a job in Berlin
and I need a favor. brother.</i>

262
00:20:20.136 --> 00:20:22.806
No problem.
I'll grab the team and meet you in Berlin.

263
00:20:23.390 --> 00:20:25.392
<i>Thanks. man. I'll see you soon.</i>

264
00:20:48.998 --> 00:20:50.000
(GRUNTS)

265
00:20:51.876 --> 00:20:54.504
You were only supposed
to create a diversion. Roman.

266
00:20:54.587 --> 00:20:55.634
That was a diversion!

267
00:20:55.714 --> 00:20:57.465
How many of the damn explosives did you use?

268
00:20:57.882 --> 00:20:59.134
ROMAN: I don't know. Tej.

269
00:20:59.217 --> 00:21:00.719
- All of it?
- Wait. all of it?

270
00:21:00.885 --> 00:21:02.804
Roman. Jesus Christ.

271
00:21:02.929 --> 00:21:04.556
We got more of your fan club ahead.

272
00:21:11.021 --> 00:21:12.063
They're still on us!

273
00:21:12.897 --> 00:21:14.232
These guys are taking this personal.

274
00:21:14.524 --> 00:21:17.656
Roman. we just blew up their facility
and stole their EMP.

275
00:21:17.736 --> 00:21:21.489
Other than your doctor's cold finger.
I'd say it's about as personal as it can get.

276
00:21:21.906 --> 00:21:23.033
Phase Two!

277
00:21:23.116 --> 00:21:25.702
Phase Two? So you just
gonna keep that to yourself?

278
00:21:25.869 --> 00:21:28.496
What happened to Phase One?
What about that part?

279
00:21:28.663 --> 00:21:30.040
Yeah. Remember the airplane?

280
00:21:30.206 --> 00:21:31.666
Everyone drove their cars out but you?

281
00:21:32.167 --> 00:21:34.002
I told you. my engine seized up.

282
00:21:34.169 --> 00:21:35.295
It's your balls that seized up.

283
00:21:35.462 --> 00:21:36.629
Just follow my lead. okay?

284
00:21:36.796 --> 00:21:39.215
And. Roman. whatever you do. don't think.

285
00:21:39.632 --> 00:21:40.633
Huh?

286
00:21:40.842 --> 00:21:42.010
Tej. drop it!

287
00:21:42.552 --> 00:21:43.720
Bombs away.

288
00:21:44.387 --> 00:21:45.388
(BEEPS)

289
00:21:45.764 --> 00:21:46.806
Split. now!

290
00:21:51.186 --> 00:21:52.437
ROMAN: Holy...

291
00:21:52.604 --> 00:21:53.772
(CURSES IN GERMAN)

292
00:22:07.786 --> 00:22:09.245
ROMAN: (OVER RADIO) <i>Great plan. Tej.</i>

293
00:22:09.621 --> 00:22:11.706
But just so you know. you missed some.

294
00:22:11.915 --> 00:22:13.416
Oh. just wait for it.

295
00:22:26.096 --> 00:22:28.098
ROMAN: Oh. shit!

296
00:22:29.891 --> 00:22:31.059
I hate you. Tej!

297
00:22:31.476 --> 00:22:32.769
(LAUGHS)

298
00:22:33.311 --> 00:22:34.396
Got your ass.

299
00:22:40.652 --> 00:22:41.736
You good?

300
00:22:44.114 --> 00:22:45.573
I'll see you when it's done.

301
00:22:49.744 --> 00:22:50.870
All right. great job. team.

302
00:22:51.037 --> 00:22:52.789
Let's break off and meet me
at the safe house.

303
00:22:53.957 --> 00:22:55.291
(ENGINE REVVING)

304
00:23:07.721 --> 00:23:08.722
A hell of a job. brother.

305
00:23:08.972 --> 00:23:10.974
When we get back to the base.
the beer's on me.

306
00:23:26.656 --> 00:23:27.991
(GASPING)

307
00:23:33.079 --> 00:23:34.080
(GRUNTS)

308
00:23:35.206 --> 00:23:37.000
You lost your goddamn mind. Toretto?

309
00:23:40.754 --> 00:23:42.339
Toretto. you put hands on that thing.

310
00:23:42.422 --> 00:23:45.008
you're gonna have the whole world
gunning for you. including me.

311
00:23:47.260 --> 00:23:48.470
(DOM GRUNTS)

312
00:23:50.013 --> 00:23:53.141
I don't know what you're doing.
but you better think about this. Toretto.

313
00:23:54.142 --> 00:23:55.769
It ain't too late to stop this.

314
00:24:08.239 --> 00:24:09.532
It is now.

315
00:24:10.367 --> 00:24:12.202
(TIRES SQUEALING)

316
00:24:12.285 --> 00:24:13.453
(SIRENS BLARING)

317
00:24:14.662 --> 00:24:16.706
That sumbitch just crossed us.

318
00:24:17.082 --> 00:24:19.129
- What?
- Wait a second. what are you talking about?

319
00:24:19.209 --> 00:24:20.210
Dom took the EMP.

320
00:24:20.418 --> 00:24:21.461
Bullshit.

321
00:24:22.504 --> 00:24:23.505
Where are you?

322
00:24:23.713 --> 00:24:24.839
HOBBS: <i>It's too late for me. Get outta here.</i>

323
00:24:25.090 --> 00:24:28.802
Saw that look in his eye.
and I've seen that look before.

324
00:24:29.636 --> 00:24:31.721
Dominic Toretto just went rogue.

325
00:25:33.867 --> 00:25:35.827
TEJ:
All right. I got his phone records. y'all.

326
00:25:35.994 --> 00:25:38.371
It's a whole bunch of calls
to untraceable numbers.

327
00:25:38.580 --> 00:25:39.581
ROMAN: Burner phones. right?

328
00:25:39.748 --> 00:25:40.999
TEJ: Nah. scrambler.

329
00:25:41.166 --> 00:25:44.210
Same number. but they got some sort
of micro-router to bury the signal path.

330
00:25:44.377 --> 00:25:48.173
which means Dom is clearly communicating
with somebody that's above our pay grade.

331
00:25:48.423 --> 00:25:52.302
Look. I don't know Dom as well as you.
but if we just look at the facts.

332
00:25:52.969 --> 00:25:55.472
Dom's been having highly
encrypted conversations

333
00:25:55.638 --> 00:25:57.098
with some mysterious person.

334
00:25:58.808 --> 00:26:00.185
He took out Hobbs.

335
00:26:00.769 --> 00:26:02.520
He stole an EMP. Now he's disappeared.

336
00:26:03.396 --> 00:26:04.564
So. what are you saying?

337
00:26:04.731 --> 00:26:07.650
Maybe we should consider
the fact that Hobbs is right.

338
00:26:08.318 --> 00:26:09.569
Dom did go rogue.

339
00:26:09.652 --> 00:26:10.779
(CAR DOOR SLAMS)

340
00:26:11.029 --> 00:26:12.030
ROMAN: Letty.

341
00:26:12.155 --> 00:26:14.074
LETTY: Before you judge the man.

342
00:26:14.240 --> 00:26:17.327
remember. you're breathing right
now because he saved your life.

343
00:26:25.669 --> 00:26:27.671
You just gonna let her bump
your shoulder like that?

344
00:26:28.421 --> 00:26:31.633
I'm just saying.
that was a little aggressive.

345
00:26:34.010 --> 00:26:35.178
What you gonna do. email her?

346
00:26:35.595 --> 00:26:36.596
(SIGHS)

347
00:26:38.598 --> 00:26:39.641
(WHISPERS) Check.

348
00:26:40.433 --> 00:26:42.185
(CELL DOOR BUZZING)

349
00:26:50.777 --> 00:26:51.903
Moment. will you. fellas?

350
00:26:53.321 --> 00:26:54.614
Thank you.

351
00:26:54.781 --> 00:26:56.199
Well. this is an exciting new look.

352
00:26:56.741 --> 00:26:58.910
It's a little tight in the crotch. as always.

353
00:26:58.993 --> 00:26:59.994
(CHUCKLES)

354
00:27:00.286 --> 00:27:02.330
What boy-band bus did she fall out of?

355
00:27:02.997 --> 00:27:04.332
It's my new junior associate.

356
00:27:04.499 --> 00:27:06.418
He's working with me on this. All yours.

357
00:27:06.501 --> 00:27:08.962
Mr. Nobody and I have been given
the authority to get you out of this.

358
00:27:09.379 --> 00:27:12.298
All you have to do is agree
to the terms and you're free.

359
00:27:13.466 --> 00:27:15.301
What's training wheels talking about?
What terms?

360
00:27:15.927 --> 00:27:17.512
Confess to your crimes in Berlin.

361
00:27:17.971 --> 00:27:21.850
Treason. international espionage.
massive destruction of civic property.

362
00:27:22.100 --> 00:27:23.685
You do that. we close the case.

363
00:27:24.102 --> 00:27:26.229
- And?
- And the DSS blacklists you.

364
00:27:26.396 --> 00:27:27.731
Germany loves that.

365
00:27:27.897 --> 00:27:29.482
LITTLE NOBODY:
Officially. you will be a criminal.

366
00:27:29.566 --> 00:27:30.567
MR. NOBODY: Wait. Whoa. whoa. whoa.

367
00:27:30.650 --> 00:27:32.360
You need to work on your delivery. all right?

368
00:27:32.569 --> 00:27:33.945
Unofficially...

369
00:27:35.405 --> 00:27:37.907
You're off the books. You come work with me.

370
00:27:39.576 --> 00:27:40.577
I'm not a criminal.

371
00:27:40.660 --> 00:27:42.162
MR. NOBODY: Luke. come on. Labels.

372
00:27:42.912 --> 00:27:44.289
There is no confession.

373
00:27:44.706 --> 00:27:46.291
There are no backroom deals.

374
00:27:46.374 --> 00:27:48.543
I got myself into this.
I'm gonna get myself out of it.

375
00:27:48.752 --> 00:27:51.087
- You know that.
- I do. and that's what I told him. (SIGHS)

376
00:27:51.338 --> 00:27:52.922
Well. there you have it.

377
00:27:54.257 --> 00:27:55.342
Good luck in the courts. man.

378
00:27:58.011 --> 00:27:59.012
What about your daughter?

379
00:28:01.931 --> 00:28:05.268
You know. if you're not gonna do it for
your country. at least do it for your kid.

380
00:28:05.435 --> 00:28:07.103
(CHUCKLES) Big mistake. kid.

381
00:28:08.355 --> 00:28:09.522
(EXCLAIMS)

382
00:28:09.606 --> 00:28:11.236
Hold on. Luke. Luke.

383
00:28:11.316 --> 00:28:13.026
He's still working from the manual.

384
00:28:13.193 --> 00:28:15.111
I mean. he doesn't even
really know the rules.

385
00:28:15.987 --> 00:28:17.322
Now. come on. give him a break.

386
00:28:17.781 --> 00:28:19.616
(STRAINED) Give me a break.

387
00:28:19.866 --> 00:28:20.867
Luke.

388
00:28:22.035 --> 00:28:23.244
(GRUNTING)

389
00:28:23.453 --> 00:28:24.454
Appreciate it.

390
00:28:24.621 --> 00:28:25.830
(COUGHING)

391
00:28:26.122 --> 00:28:27.540
It's good to see you. Nobody.

392
00:28:27.707 --> 00:28:28.833
You. too.

393
00:28:31.628 --> 00:28:32.962
Rule number one...

394
00:28:34.297 --> 00:28:35.507
Know your audience.

395
00:28:35.674 --> 00:28:37.884
I gave you your shot. You shit the bed.

396
00:28:38.051 --> 00:28:39.969
Now I'm gonna show you how to get this done.

397
00:28:40.512 --> 00:28:42.681
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

398
00:28:48.812 --> 00:28:50.689
You're dead. cop. Dead!

399
00:28:50.855 --> 00:28:53.233
INMATE: I'm gonna slice
some bacon off your back. pig.

400
00:28:54.693 --> 00:28:56.486
DECKARD: Well. well. well...

401
00:28:56.653 --> 00:29:00.407
Luke Hobbs behind bars.
Would you look at that.

402
00:29:01.408 --> 00:29:03.201
The bent cop got his day.

403
00:29:04.494 --> 00:29:06.329
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

404
00:29:07.163 --> 00:29:08.164
(CELL DOOR BUZZING)

405
00:29:16.506 --> 00:29:17.882
You know. that color looks good on you.

406
00:29:18.049 --> 00:29:20.260
Yeah. it'll look a whole hell of a lot
better with your blood on it.

407
00:29:20.593 --> 00:29:22.262
Yeah. good luck with that. Hercules.

408
00:29:23.054 --> 00:29:24.556
Lawman gone bad. huh?

409
00:29:25.515 --> 00:29:26.850
Such a cliche.

410
00:29:27.851 --> 00:29:29.519
Oh. well. welcome to the club.

411
00:29:30.228 --> 00:29:32.022
I wouldn't get that twisted. son.

412
00:29:32.188 --> 00:29:34.190
We ain't in no club.
we got nothing in common.

413
00:29:34.274 --> 00:29:35.942
And unlike you. I ain't gonna be here long.

414
00:29:36.192 --> 00:29:37.318
What. you bring a shovel. did you?

415
00:29:37.902 --> 00:29:40.363
Because it's 38 feet of steel and concrete.

416
00:29:40.947 --> 00:29:42.157
Or so I've been told.

417
00:29:42.532 --> 00:29:43.867
(DECKARD CHUCKLES)

418
00:29:44.451 --> 00:29:45.702
Better get to digging.

419
00:29:47.078 --> 00:29:48.079
Wanker.

420
00:29:51.166 --> 00:29:52.250
Yeah.

421
00:30:09.559 --> 00:30:10.769
Move.

422
00:30:11.519 --> 00:30:12.979
Say that again.

423
00:30:13.605 --> 00:30:17.359
If I say it again. it'll be to a corpse.

424
00:30:18.777 --> 00:30:19.986
(CHUCKLES)

425
00:30:20.653 --> 00:30:21.988
I'm gonna enjoy this.

426
00:30:22.489 --> 00:30:23.573
CIPHER: Welcome back. Dom.

427
00:30:24.032 --> 00:30:25.075
Nice job out there.

428
00:30:26.868 --> 00:30:28.286
You excited about tonight?

429
00:30:29.829 --> 00:30:30.830
You're going on this?

430
00:30:36.127 --> 00:30:37.420
You're with me. Dom.

431
00:30:47.389 --> 00:30:48.807
Showing me your shoe collection?

432
00:30:49.099 --> 00:30:50.100
Yep.

433
00:30:53.520 --> 00:30:55.313
A pair for every occasion.

434
00:30:55.480 --> 00:30:58.358
You have enough guns in here
to outfit a small army. huh?

435
00:30:58.525 --> 00:31:00.652
Oh. this is just the tip of the iceberg.

436
00:31:03.905 --> 00:31:06.908
You know what I like about you. Dom?
You're a genuine outlaw.

437
00:31:07.200 --> 00:31:09.661
I mean. you're a man
who lives by his own rules.

438
00:31:09.953 --> 00:31:12.542
Which is surprising.
because when I saw you in Cuba.

439
00:31:12.622 --> 00:31:15.917
I heard about a guy who almost
killed you with a motorcycle.

440
00:31:16.126 --> 00:31:18.670
and you let him keep his car?

441
00:31:19.212 --> 00:31:20.797
Oh. that confused you?

442
00:31:21.172 --> 00:31:22.173
Hmm.

443
00:31:23.967 --> 00:31:25.885
'Course I could've taken his car.

444
00:31:26.553 --> 00:31:28.179
But it's about something bigger.

445
00:31:28.888 --> 00:31:30.306
This way...

446
00:31:32.100 --> 00:31:33.101
I changed him.

447
00:31:33.309 --> 00:31:34.811
That's not your responsibility.

448
00:31:35.061 --> 00:31:36.813
- But it's who I am.
- Is it?

449
00:31:37.397 --> 00:31:39.941
Let me ask you something. Dom.
What's the best thing in your life?

450
00:31:41.609 --> 00:31:43.278
- Family.
- No. it's not.

451
00:31:45.321 --> 00:31:46.865
Not if you're being honest.

452
00:31:47.699 --> 00:31:50.410
It's the 10 seconds between start and finish.

453
00:31:50.493 --> 00:31:52.328
when you're not thinking about anything.

454
00:31:52.662 --> 00:31:55.331
No family. no obligations.

455
00:31:55.498 --> 00:31:56.750
Just you.

456
00:31:57.834 --> 00:31:58.835
Being free.

457
00:32:04.174 --> 00:32:05.258
I gotta tell you.

458
00:32:05.342 --> 00:32:09.512
this whole saving-the-world. Robin Hood
nonsense you've been doing recently?

459
00:32:09.846 --> 00:32:12.265
It's bullshit. It's not you.

460
00:32:17.812 --> 00:32:19.439
Be who you are.

461
00:32:20.065 --> 00:32:22.067
Why live only a quarter mile at a time

462
00:32:22.150 --> 00:32:24.778
when you can live your whole life that way?

463
00:32:27.822 --> 00:32:29.115
(PANTING)

464
00:32:36.206 --> 00:32:37.290
Is that it?

465
00:32:37.874 --> 00:32:40.377
Is that all those
bloated-out muscles will give ya?

466
00:32:40.877 --> 00:32:42.420
All show and no go.

467
00:32:42.796 --> 00:32:43.880
(GRUNTS)

468
00:32:48.009 --> 00:32:49.344
(GRUNTING)

469
00:32:56.518 --> 00:32:57.602
Oh. I got plenty of go.

470
00:32:57.977 --> 00:33:02.315
You must've misplaced that when I kicked
your arse up and down that office of yours.

471
00:33:02.399 --> 00:33:03.400
Yeah.

472
00:33:05.402 --> 00:33:07.529
Just like you Brits. rewriting history. huh?

473
00:33:07.737 --> 00:33:10.990
All I know is. it wasn't me that was
thrown out of a four-story window.

474
00:33:11.074 --> 00:33:12.117
Jumped.

475
00:33:12.200 --> 00:33:15.078
I jumped out of a four-story window.
saving my partner's life.

476
00:33:15.954 --> 00:33:19.290
'Cause where I'm from.
we don't settle fights by throwing bombs.

477
00:33:19.374 --> 00:33:23.086
Well. that's funny. because where I'm from.
we don't need women to run to our rescue.

478
00:33:23.837 --> 00:33:26.673
I mean. do you really believe
you can stand in front of me

479
00:33:27.924 --> 00:33:30.218
and beat me in a straight-up.
old-fashioned fist fight?

480
00:33:30.385 --> 00:33:31.594
Let me tell you something.

481
00:33:32.095 --> 00:33:35.932
Me and you. one-on-one. no one else around.

482
00:33:36.599 --> 00:33:40.729
I will beat your ass like a Cherokee drum.

483
00:33:43.690 --> 00:33:45.108
Maybe one day we'll find out.

484
00:33:45.608 --> 00:33:47.485
Oh. you better hope that day never comes.

485
00:33:47.569 --> 00:33:49.237
(DOOR BUZZES)

486
00:33:57.412 --> 00:34:00.665
I said no. Mr. Nobody.
I'm not leaving this cell.

487
00:34:01.207 --> 00:34:02.459
I'll get out my way.

488
00:34:02.625 --> 00:34:03.752
(ALARM BLARING)

489
00:34:03.918 --> 00:34:04.919
The right way!

490
00:34:09.799 --> 00:34:11.134
Hey! Why's the door open?
Get back in your cell!

491
00:34:11.217 --> 00:34:12.802
Relax. It's just a malfunction.

492
00:34:12.969 --> 00:34:14.766
- Get back!
- HOBBS: Just a malfunction.

493
00:34:14.846 --> 00:34:16.097
(GRUNTING)

494
00:34:24.147 --> 00:34:25.482
(GRUNTING)

495
00:34:26.983 --> 00:34:28.818
Stop him! Don't let him get away!

496
00:34:29.652 --> 00:34:30.737
(GRUNTING)

497
00:34:31.821 --> 00:34:32.989
(GROANING)

498
00:34:34.157 --> 00:34:35.575
(GRUNTING)

499
00:34:57.847 --> 00:34:59.015
(YELLING)

500
00:35:02.352 --> 00:35:03.478
MILLER: Hobbs!

501
00:35:04.979 --> 00:35:06.815
I've been waiting a long time for this.

502
00:35:07.982 --> 00:35:09.192
Keep waiting. bitch.

503
00:35:09.275 --> 00:35:10.360
(GRUNTS)

504
00:35:13.363 --> 00:35:14.406
(GROANS)

505
00:35:14.489 --> 00:35:16.700
Rubber bullets. Big mistake.

506
00:35:23.289 --> 00:35:24.457
(GROANING)

507
00:35:32.549 --> 00:35:33.550
(YELLS)

508
00:35:49.399 --> 00:35:50.567
(GRUNTING)

509
00:36:14.716 --> 00:36:16.134
(ALL GRUNTING)

510
00:36:31.441 --> 00:36:33.026
(BOTH PANTING)

511
00:36:38.823 --> 00:36:40.950
Well. that took longer than I expected.

512
00:36:43.161 --> 00:36:44.287
- HOBBS: <i>Two questions.</i>
- MR. NOBODY: <i>Yeah.</i>

513
00:36:44.537 --> 00:36:46.456
- My daughter?
- With your sister.

514
00:36:47.290 --> 00:36:48.920
- Toretto?
- (CHUCKLES)

515
00:36:49.000 --> 00:36:50.710
It's interesting you ask.

516
00:36:51.670 --> 00:36:54.214
This is my new base. Welcome to nowhere.

517
00:36:54.798 --> 00:36:56.094
It's a little sterile for you.

518
00:36:56.174 --> 00:36:57.262
(CHUCKLES)

519
00:36:57.342 --> 00:36:59.219
Listen. there's something
I wanna talk to you about after.

520
00:36:59.302 --> 00:37:00.679
Hey. listen. guys. Thanks...

521
00:37:00.762 --> 00:37:02.931
Whoa. whoa. whoa.
What? Handcuffs? What is this?

522
00:37:03.139 --> 00:37:04.561
It's called abuse of power.

523
00:37:04.641 --> 00:37:05.934
You told me to round them up.

524
00:37:06.142 --> 00:37:07.185
I didn't tell you to hand...

525
00:37:08.311 --> 00:37:10.563
Cut 'em loose. Oh. man. This is embarrassing.

526
00:37:11.022 --> 00:37:12.482
I'm sorry. guys. really. I...

527
00:37:13.316 --> 00:37:14.693
So. this is how you treat old friends?

528
00:37:14.984 --> 00:37:18.321
TEJ: Friends? We don't even really know
who the hell this guy is.

529
00:37:18.488 --> 00:37:20.532
Doesn't matter who I am. Tej.
I'm. like. nobody. okay?

530
00:37:20.824 --> 00:37:22.033
Nobody. So. then. who is he?

531
00:37:22.200 --> 00:37:23.910
Him? He's nothing. He's. like. less than me.

532
00:37:23.993 --> 00:37:26.996
Clearly. we're getting nowhere with nobody.

533
00:37:27.497 --> 00:37:30.000
I've been in here for four hours.
and my ribs are showing.

534
00:37:30.667 --> 00:37:32.836
I don't know about y'all. but I'm out.

535
00:37:34.337 --> 00:37:35.922
- I wouldn't recommend that.
- What?

536
00:37:36.006 --> 00:37:38.508
Well. thanks to your botched Berlin job.

537
00:37:38.591 --> 00:37:40.844
you all made Interpol's
Top 10 Most Wanted list.

538
00:37:41.011 --> 00:37:42.178
- Top 10.
- MR. NOBODY: Mmm-hmm.

539
00:37:42.887 --> 00:37:43.888
That's all right.

540
00:37:43.972 --> 00:37:46.645
- Well. not you. Roman.
- What do you mean?

541
00:37:46.725 --> 00:37:49.102
You just missed the cut.
You're number 11. so...

542
00:37:49.185 --> 00:37:51.271
- I'm... I missed?
- Yeah.

543
00:37:51.855 --> 00:37:52.897
ROMAN: That's impossible!

544
00:37:53.606 --> 00:37:54.858
What number did they come in at?

545
00:37:56.026 --> 00:37:59.237
Six. eight. nine. ten.

546
00:38:00.363 --> 00:38:01.451
- She's 10?
- Mmm-hmm.

547
00:38:01.531 --> 00:38:03.658
That's impossible. There's no way she's a 10.

548
00:38:03.825 --> 00:38:05.535
Oh. she's definitely a 10. (SCOFFS)

549
00:38:06.494 --> 00:38:10.498
How about we focus on someone who
we're not gonna find on anybody's list.

550
00:38:10.665 --> 00:38:12.459
We're awaiting hard confirmation.

551
00:38:12.542 --> 00:38:16.379
but I believe that's the cyber
terrorist known as Cipher.

552
00:38:17.172 --> 00:38:20.383
Wait. no. Cipher's an organization.
Not a person.

553
00:38:20.675 --> 00:38:21.718
Not according to our sources.

554
00:38:21.926 --> 00:38:23.011
What does she want?

555
00:38:23.136 --> 00:38:24.220
No one knows.

556
00:38:24.554 --> 00:38:26.473
Cipher is like a digital act of God.

557
00:38:26.931 --> 00:38:30.935
They... Well. she can manipulate
world systems from the shadows.

558
00:38:31.019 --> 00:38:32.691
Anything that can be hacked
is hers to play with.

559
00:38:32.771 --> 00:38:36.399
And here's the kicker.
You'll never find her linked to any of it.

560
00:38:36.524 --> 00:38:39.778
Her digital identity is scrubbed
every few seconds. worldwide.

561
00:38:39.861 --> 00:38:41.196
So. basically. she's the bogeyman.

562
00:38:41.363 --> 00:38:44.449
Damn. she's one of the hottest
bogeymans I've ever seen.

563
00:38:44.741 --> 00:38:47.410
I mean. if y'all know her.
tell her to get at your boy.

564
00:38:47.494 --> 00:38:49.162
- (ROMAN CHUCKLES)
- (CLEARS THROAT)

565
00:38:49.537 --> 00:38:51.414
- What are you. 12?
- ROMAN: That was my shin. mother...

566
00:38:51.581 --> 00:38:55.251
Let's just say. people are scared
of the hacker group Anonymous.

567
00:38:55.418 --> 00:38:56.840
But even Anonymous won't mess with her.

568
00:38:56.920 --> 00:38:59.339
What the hell does
any of this have to do with us?

569
00:38:59.422 --> 00:39:02.053
Probably nothing. Letty.
but I do find it interesting that.

570
00:39:02.133 --> 00:39:05.929
apparently. for some reason.
she's now working with this guy.

571
00:39:20.276 --> 00:39:21.319
(SIGHS)

572
00:39:21.403 --> 00:39:25.031
He's already delivered a fully
operational EMP into her hands.

573
00:39:25.407 --> 00:39:29.285
Detonate that. they can turn any city
in the world into a war zone.

574
00:39:29.703 --> 00:39:32.163
So. then. what is it you're suggesting we do?

575
00:39:32.247 --> 00:39:33.415
MR. NOBODY: Maybe we find Dom. huh?

576
00:39:33.581 --> 00:39:36.668
Well. first. let's catch him.
and then figure out why he's turned.

577
00:39:37.127 --> 00:39:39.838
So. y'all want us to track Dom.

578
00:39:40.005 --> 00:39:42.215
Yeah. I know. Roman. it's kind of a big job.

579
00:39:42.674 --> 00:39:43.758
It's impossible.

580
00:39:43.925 --> 00:39:48.221
Which is why I'm bringing in
an extra pair of hands.

581
00:39:54.394 --> 00:39:56.813
Ah. my day just got
a whole hell of a lot better.

582
00:39:56.980 --> 00:39:58.276
Mr. Nobody. you wanna tell me why

583
00:39:58.356 --> 00:40:02.819
you just put me in a room with this
tea-and-crumpets eating. criminal sumbitch?

584
00:40:02.902 --> 00:40:07.285
What a big mouth on a small head.
coming from Prisoner 6753.

585
00:40:07.365 --> 00:40:09.454
Don't think we've forgotten
everything that you've done.

586
00:40:09.534 --> 00:40:11.957
We are not teaming up with this guy.

587
00:40:12.037 --> 00:40:14.622
Let's get one thing clear.
I ain't on your team.

588
00:40:15.081 --> 00:40:18.335
I don't care about you.
your crew. or your little family.

589
00:40:18.710 --> 00:40:19.798
I'm here for Cipher.

590
00:40:19.878 --> 00:40:21.713
What are you gonna do.
apply for a job? Head Asshole?

591
00:40:21.963 --> 00:40:24.924
You know. I think that tight T-shirt's
cutting off the circulation to your brain.

592
00:40:25.008 --> 00:40:26.259
You should get a bigger size.

593
00:40:26.968 --> 00:40:30.475
Cipher came to me first.
Wanted me to steal Nightshade for her.

594
00:40:30.555 --> 00:40:32.057
When I said no. she went after my brother.

595
00:40:32.140 --> 00:40:35.352
Ah. yes. brother Owen.
Who could forget him. huh?

596
00:40:36.019 --> 00:40:38.483
Former hell-raiser and current guest

597
00:40:38.563 --> 00:40:41.149
at a nasty little black site prison.

598
00:40:41.566 --> 00:40:43.488
Cipher corrupted him and left him for dead.

599
00:40:43.568 --> 00:40:46.157
So. if I get a shot to take her down.
believe me. Flex. I'm taking it.

600
00:40:46.237 --> 00:40:48.159
You're taking my boot right up your ass.
is what you're taking.

601
00:40:48.239 --> 00:40:50.996
Guys. guys. The fastest way
to find Cipher is through Toretto.

602
00:40:51.076 --> 00:40:53.456
Now. aside from myself.
there's only two men in the world

603
00:40:53.536 --> 00:40:55.872
that have ever managed to actually
track him down with any success.

604
00:40:56.039 --> 00:40:58.837
And guess what. They're both
standing in front of me right now.

605
00:40:58.917 --> 00:41:01.920
So. like it or not.
you two are gonna work together.

606
00:41:02.921 --> 00:41:04.089
You got that?

607
00:41:07.008 --> 00:41:08.218
I'm gonna take that as a yes.

608
00:41:09.552 --> 00:41:11.012
Am I the only one seeing this?

609
00:41:11.805 --> 00:41:13.223
Oh. this ought to be good.

610
00:41:13.306 --> 00:41:14.474
(MUMBLES)

611
00:41:16.393 --> 00:41:17.519
Use God's Eye.

612
00:41:18.103 --> 00:41:19.562
We put our lives on the line.

613
00:41:19.646 --> 00:41:22.482
running around the world
trying to figure this thing out.

614
00:41:22.565 --> 00:41:23.942
It can find anybody. right?

615
00:41:24.567 --> 00:41:26.069
Let's use it to find Dom.

616
00:41:26.403 --> 00:41:29.406
Roman. that is a great idea.

617
00:41:30.365 --> 00:41:32.784
Did you hear that? "Great idea."

618
00:41:33.201 --> 00:41:34.577
No. no. no. don't tune it out. Huh?

619
00:41:34.994 --> 00:41:36.871
Mr. Nobody. let's fire it up. huh?

620
00:41:48.258 --> 00:41:49.926
TEJ: Got him. He's in London.

621
00:41:52.178 --> 00:41:53.179
Yeah.

622
00:41:53.263 --> 00:41:54.556
(BEEPING)

623
00:41:55.932 --> 00:41:59.269
RAMSEY:
Wait. We've got a second match in Hong Kong.

624
00:41:59.436 --> 00:42:01.980
ROMAN: Beijing and Seoul.

625
00:42:02.063 --> 00:42:03.565
TEJ: And Tokyo.

626
00:42:05.191 --> 00:42:07.986
RAMSEY: And just about every
other major city on the planet.

627
00:42:08.069 --> 00:42:11.573
MR. NOBODY:
And so. God's Eye was where we started.

628
00:42:11.698 --> 00:42:13.533
But Cipher's already created an evasion

629
00:42:13.616 --> 00:42:17.704
that masks their location by pinging
random spots all over the globe.

630
00:42:17.787 --> 00:42:19.372
but it was a good thought. Roman.

631
00:42:20.749 --> 00:42:22.375
So. she's made my program obsolete.

632
00:42:22.459 --> 00:42:24.794
And that. Ramsey. is why you're here.

633
00:42:25.295 --> 00:42:27.797
See. simple solutions
aren't gonna cut it here. slick.

634
00:42:30.133 --> 00:42:31.593
Why you look at me when you say that?

635
00:42:32.010 --> 00:42:34.721
Wait a second. Wait. wait.
Simple solutions might just cut it.

636
00:42:35.138 --> 00:42:38.436
You see. in order for God's Eye
to give off all these false pings.

637
00:42:38.516 --> 00:42:40.435
means they have to be using a FLEA relay.

638
00:42:40.643 --> 00:42:41.686
Watch these two.

639
00:42:41.770 --> 00:42:43.855
Which means it has
a decaying sync randomizer.

640
00:42:43.938 --> 00:42:45.110
Which we can reverse...

641
00:42:45.190 --> 00:42:49.277
And track it back to the originating source
and find Dom's true location.

642
00:42:50.445 --> 00:42:51.738
I'm telling you. they got skills.

643
00:42:52.155 --> 00:42:53.365
That was my idea.

644
00:42:53.907 --> 00:42:55.575
That's what I was saying. Remember in there?

645
00:42:55.658 --> 00:42:57.243
All right. let's try this.

646
00:43:07.837 --> 00:43:08.838
It's working.

647
00:43:09.297 --> 00:43:12.509
Time you wanna check your manual
and start organizing a force response.

648
00:43:13.510 --> 00:43:14.844
Let's get a hold of
our international assets...

649
00:43:14.928 --> 00:43:16.346
He's still green.

650
00:43:16.429 --> 00:43:18.264
Yeah. like fresh baby shit.

651
00:43:18.348 --> 00:43:20.934
As soon as we have Toretto's location.
I want to mobilize.

652
00:43:23.520 --> 00:43:26.147
Let's get a hold of a better asshole.

653
00:43:26.272 --> 00:43:28.441
No one respects you...
(IMITATES RADIO STATIC) Cover.

654
00:43:28.608 --> 00:43:29.609
Get away from me.

655
00:43:30.360 --> 00:43:31.569
All right. they're not in China.

656
00:43:33.029 --> 00:43:34.030
Or Russia.

657
00:43:35.490 --> 00:43:36.616
Europe's clear.

658
00:43:38.201 --> 00:43:39.953
But this one's not going away.

659
00:43:40.078 --> 00:43:41.371
(BEEPING)

660
00:43:41.621 --> 00:43:42.664
This is interesting.

661
00:43:44.040 --> 00:43:45.041
Why?

662
00:43:45.208 --> 00:43:46.835
(BEEPING RAPIDLY)

663
00:43:47.043 --> 00:43:48.253
Because that's here.

664
00:43:49.004 --> 00:43:50.338
(GRUNTING)

665
00:44:03.059 --> 00:44:04.561
(GRUNTING)

666
00:44:10.525 --> 00:44:11.568
(EXCLAIMS)

667
00:44:17.824 --> 00:44:19.367
(MAN COUGHING)

668
00:44:28.835 --> 00:44:30.340
CIPHER: (ECHOING) Did you all enjoy that?

669
00:44:30.420 --> 00:44:32.756
Next-generation concussion grenade.

670
00:44:33.048 --> 00:44:38.136
It scrambles your senses.
Don't worry. it'll wear off in an hour.

671
00:44:38.219 --> 00:44:39.804
- (GROANING)
- Probably.

672
00:44:40.472 --> 00:44:42.682
Hello. Deckard. Nice to see you again.

673
00:44:45.560 --> 00:44:48.396
(LAUGHING) Look at this.
body's not even cold. Dom.

674
00:44:48.688 --> 00:44:50.940
Your family's already replacing you.

675
00:44:52.859 --> 00:44:54.778
You chose the losing team.

676
00:44:55.945 --> 00:44:58.531
I guess your brother is smarter than you.

677
00:45:02.494 --> 00:45:03.578
(DECKARD GRUNTING)

678
00:45:27.811 --> 00:45:29.145
(BEEPING)

679
00:45:32.565 --> 00:45:35.068
Smart move. embedding God's Eye
into the mainframe.

680
00:45:35.527 --> 00:45:38.822
Irritating to make me have to come
all the way down here to get it. but...

681
00:45:42.450 --> 00:45:43.576
Let's go.

682
00:45:43.910 --> 00:45:45.620
(ALL GROANING)

683
00:45:50.333 --> 00:45:51.459
Dom!

684
00:46:00.510 --> 00:46:03.972
You're gonna turn your back
on family? Just like that?

685
00:46:39.466 --> 00:46:40.967
Let's go.

686
00:47:00.403 --> 00:47:02.197
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

687
00:47:14.250 --> 00:47:15.418
HOBBS: You okay?

688
00:47:18.922 --> 00:47:19.923
That wasn't him.

689
00:47:23.802 --> 00:47:28.390
I don't know what she's got on him.
but that wasn't Dom.

690
00:47:30.183 --> 00:47:31.521
Brian would know what to do.

691
00:47:31.601 --> 00:47:32.727
No!

692
00:47:36.648 --> 00:47:39.067
We can't bring Brian and Mia into this.

693
00:47:39.609 --> 00:47:41.027
We agreed on that.

694
00:47:43.488 --> 00:47:44.572
ROMAN: I know.

695
00:47:52.622 --> 00:47:57.293
DOM: Back there. was that for her.
for me. or you?

696
00:47:58.294 --> 00:48:00.714
And was it even necessary?

697
00:48:01.548 --> 00:48:03.550
Necessary?

698
00:48:03.717 --> 00:48:05.135
Nothing is necessary.

699
00:48:05.301 --> 00:48:07.470
Everything is a choice.

700
00:48:07.637 --> 00:48:09.973
And I simply made one. But so did you.

701
00:48:10.181 --> 00:48:12.308
You could've stopped me.
but you chose not to.

702
00:48:12.517 --> 00:48:14.686
I wonder what Letty thought about that.

703
00:48:17.230 --> 00:48:19.524
The problem with putting
your foot on a tiger's neck

704
00:48:19.691 --> 00:48:21.151
is you can never let it up.

705
00:48:21.651 --> 00:48:25.947
I think I need to remind you
why you chose to be here.

706
00:48:51.139 --> 00:48:52.140
(GASPS)

707
00:48:52.849 --> 00:48:54.017
Elena.

708
00:49:01.358 --> 00:49:02.484
ELENA: Dom?

709
00:49:09.366 --> 00:49:10.867
I'm sorry.

710
00:49:13.536 --> 00:49:14.662
You shouldn't have come.

711
00:49:15.747 --> 00:49:17.874
Nothing could have kept me away.

712
00:49:18.041 --> 00:49:19.584
Now she has the three of us.

713
00:49:20.794 --> 00:49:22.003
(BABY COOING)

714
00:49:26.216 --> 00:49:28.009
Do you wanna see him?

715
00:49:32.263 --> 00:49:33.518
See Papa?

716
00:49:33.598 --> 00:49:34.933
(BABY GURGLING)

717
00:49:36.101 --> 00:49:37.519
See Papa.

718
00:49:41.398 --> 00:49:42.732
Papa.

719
00:49:46.611 --> 00:49:47.862
(COOING)

720
00:49:52.742 --> 00:49:56.871
When I realized I was pregnant.
you had just found out Letty was alive.

721
00:49:58.790 --> 00:50:01.918
So I decided when Letty and you got
back from your honeymoon.

722
00:50:02.085 --> 00:50:03.920
I was going to tell you.

723
00:50:06.214 --> 00:50:09.342
But then she took us before I had the chance.

724
00:50:09.426 --> 00:50:10.635
(COOS)

725
00:50:14.431 --> 00:50:15.598
His name?

726
00:50:17.267 --> 00:50:18.309
(CONTINUES COOING)

727
00:50:18.393 --> 00:50:20.186
I call him Marcos.

728
00:50:21.730 --> 00:50:23.732
But that's his middle name.

729
00:50:24.899 --> 00:50:28.445
I thought his father
should give him his first name.

730
00:50:37.412 --> 00:50:39.456
I'm sorry. Dom.

731
00:50:40.582 --> 00:50:42.751
There's nothing to be sorry for.

732
00:50:45.545 --> 00:50:46.796
ELENA: Whatever happens.

733
00:50:48.631 --> 00:50:50.592
just save our son.

734
00:50:54.471 --> 00:50:56.222
Your son.

735
00:51:16.993 --> 00:51:18.745
CIPHER: Good visit?

736
00:51:20.997 --> 00:51:23.667
I know. I know what you're thinking.

737
00:51:25.335 --> 00:51:29.172
I just let the guards go. so there's
only two opponents in the room.

738
00:51:29.506 --> 00:51:32.509
Rhodes has the gun.
so you'll take him out first.

739
00:51:32.676 --> 00:51:33.802
I know you.

740
00:51:34.135 --> 00:51:37.305
And then you're thinking. Elena's a cop.

741
00:51:37.472 --> 00:51:40.684
Maybe the two of you
can fight your way out of here.

742
00:51:40.850 --> 00:51:43.019
(WHISPERS) So much to think about.

743
00:51:43.269 --> 00:51:45.063
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

744
00:51:48.650 --> 00:51:50.527
Let me make it easier for you.

745
00:51:57.242 --> 00:51:59.119
Do with it as you wish.

746
00:52:07.168 --> 00:52:09.379
Have you heard of Choice Theory. Dom?

747
00:52:09.713 --> 00:52:11.214
There is a bunch of axioms.

748
00:52:11.381 --> 00:52:14.050
but only two you really need
to concern yourself with.

749
00:52:14.217 --> 00:52:18.888
One. the only person's behavior
we can control is our own.

750
00:52:19.055 --> 00:52:23.309
And. two. the only thing we can truly give
another person is information.

751
00:52:23.476 --> 00:52:25.395
So. let me give you some.

752
00:52:26.479 --> 00:52:27.939
You see these cameras in here?

753
00:52:29.566 --> 00:52:32.485
The moment you make a move.
highly-paid men with weapons

754
00:52:32.652 --> 00:52:34.988
will make their way into this room

755
00:52:35.071 --> 00:52:37.615
with one very specific instruction.

756
00:52:38.324 --> 00:52:39.951
It's not to save me.

757
00:52:41.619 --> 00:52:43.455
It's to kill your son.

758
00:52:44.748 --> 00:52:46.791
Now. that's a lot of bullets.

759
00:52:46.958 --> 00:52:49.627
and it only takes one
for you to lose everything.

760
00:52:49.794 --> 00:52:52.422
So. I have to ask you.

761
00:52:52.589 --> 00:52:55.884
because I know family is so important to you.

762
00:52:58.636 --> 00:53:01.514
Is that really a choice you want to make?

763
00:53:05.060 --> 00:53:07.103
Because I'm ready if you are.

764
00:53:10.815 --> 00:53:13.943
If I pull this trigger.
and God knows I want to.

765
00:53:14.944 --> 00:53:19.699
if I killed everyone on this plane.
I still couldn't get in there.

766
00:53:20.700 --> 00:53:23.536
'Cause of your two-man fail-safe system.

767
00:53:24.579 --> 00:53:26.247
Since I'm alone.

768
00:53:28.833 --> 00:53:31.086
I got no choice!

769
00:53:39.844 --> 00:53:42.013
I didn't think so.

770
00:54:12.794 --> 00:54:15.130
You want to see the old Dom?

771
00:54:17.465 --> 00:54:18.675
Watch.

772
00:54:25.348 --> 00:54:26.683
(SOBBING)

773
00:54:28.059 --> 00:54:29.185
Bitch.

774
00:54:30.729 --> 00:54:32.689
- Don't. don't.
- Sweet dreams.

775
00:54:32.856 --> 00:54:34.024
Please!

776
00:54:37.777 --> 00:54:38.862
LITTLE NOBODY: Damn it.

777
00:54:39.529 --> 00:54:41.740
She wiped it all. Took God's Eye.

778
00:54:42.574 --> 00:54:45.243
That was the one thing
we could use to find them.

779
00:54:45.410 --> 00:54:46.703
We lost everything.

780
00:54:49.039 --> 00:54:50.040
What do you got. Princess?

781
00:54:51.291 --> 00:54:53.001
Finding Toretto.

782
00:54:53.460 --> 00:54:55.211
But I got a couple of minutes to spare.

783
00:54:55.378 --> 00:54:58.089
if you want me to send you
to the hospital. Again.

784
00:54:58.423 --> 00:55:00.342
(CHUCKLES) Yo. Rules.

785
00:55:00.508 --> 00:55:02.135
First off. that's not my name.

786
00:55:02.427 --> 00:55:04.304
- Little Nobody.
- Don't call me that.

787
00:55:04.471 --> 00:55:05.472
Oh. that's definitely sticking.

788
00:55:05.555 --> 00:55:08.687
Great. Do me a favor and tell Your Majesty
over there that we're gonna find Toretto.

789
00:55:08.767 --> 00:55:10.518
We find Toretto together as a team.

790
00:55:10.602 --> 00:55:11.811
And when this is all over with.

791
00:55:11.978 --> 00:55:14.356
I'm happy to slap that
whisker biscuit right off his face.

792
00:55:14.522 --> 00:55:16.733
Wait a minute. guys.
I think Deckard's actually onto something.

793
00:55:16.900 --> 00:55:20.528
How do you think Dom and Cipher
got into the country without us knowing?

794
00:55:21.404 --> 00:55:22.447
Ghost flights.

795
00:55:22.572 --> 00:55:25.450
I thought untraceable aircraft
was all Internet conspiracy stuff.

796
00:55:25.533 --> 00:55:26.576
MR. NOBODY: It's not.

797
00:55:26.701 --> 00:55:30.413
Satellites and radar grids
all across the globe

798
00:55:30.580 --> 00:55:32.665
shift like an ocean.

799
00:55:32.832 --> 00:55:34.959
They've got channels that open and close.

800
00:55:35.126 --> 00:55:38.088
And theoretically. if you know the right
people who know the right patterns...

801
00:55:38.505 --> 00:55:40.965
You can fly right through the blind
spots completely undetected.

802
00:55:41.758 --> 00:55:43.468
So you know where Dom is headed?

803
00:55:43.551 --> 00:55:44.761
(LAPTOP BEEPS)

804
00:55:44.844 --> 00:55:47.430
Yeah. New York.

805
00:55:47.514 --> 00:55:48.556
(CHUCKLES)

806
00:55:49.766 --> 00:55:50.934
You see there. Luke?

807
00:55:51.101 --> 00:55:53.144
You guys are gonna get along just great.

808
00:55:53.353 --> 00:55:57.107
Which proves rule number two.
you never lose everything.

809
00:55:57.273 --> 00:55:58.483
Fire up the chopper.

810
00:55:58.650 --> 00:56:01.111
Well. guys. have a ball in the Big Apple.

811
00:56:24.175 --> 00:56:26.219
ROMAN:
<i>And why are we traveling like this again?</i>

812
00:56:26.386 --> 00:56:29.973
TEJ: <i>Because Dom took God's Eye.
so we need to stay off the grid.</i>

813
00:56:30.348 --> 00:56:31.808
ROMAN: But like this?

814
00:56:34.019 --> 00:56:35.645
(ALL GRUNTING)

815
00:56:35.979 --> 00:56:37.108
ROMAN: Look here. man.

816
00:56:37.188 --> 00:56:40.817
Before I throw up in my mouth.
let me ask you. what are we doing here?

817
00:56:40.984 --> 00:56:42.527
That's a good question. Roman.

818
00:56:43.820 --> 00:56:45.071
Let me show you.

819
00:56:49.659 --> 00:56:52.203
Welcome to our new base of operations.

820
00:56:52.370 --> 00:56:55.498
No. seriously. What is this place?

821
00:56:55.665 --> 00:56:58.084
This is heaven.

822
00:57:04.049 --> 00:57:07.260
It's the agency garage.
They call it the Toy Shop.

823
00:57:11.556 --> 00:57:13.350
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

824
00:57:14.476 --> 00:57:16.314
LITTLE NOBODY:
This is where we house every vehicle

825
00:57:16.394 --> 00:57:18.563
seized from drug dealers on the East Coast.

826
00:57:18.730 --> 00:57:22.817
Now. Mr. Nobody said that if we're
gonna have a chance at catching Dom.

827
00:57:24.235 --> 00:57:26.363
we're gonna have to be damn fast.

828
00:57:27.572 --> 00:57:29.240
Figured this would help.

829
00:57:32.452 --> 00:57:33.828
We got a tank.

830
00:57:33.995 --> 00:57:36.122
750 horsepower.

831
00:57:36.289 --> 00:57:40.126
6.6 liter. V8 Duramax engine

832
00:57:40.293 --> 00:57:44.255
with an M153 CROWS remotely
operated weapon station on top.

833
00:57:44.422 --> 00:57:46.716
You didn't get this from drug dealers.

834
00:57:46.883 --> 00:57:50.512
LITTLE NOBODY: No. No. that. uh.
the United States Army lent me.

835
00:57:50.720 --> 00:57:54.057
See. the Army's developing machines like this
that soldiers can drive from a mile away.

836
00:57:54.224 --> 00:57:56.768
so they can stay safe and alive.

837
00:57:56.935 --> 00:57:59.604
But. luckily. there's a backup driver's seat

838
00:57:59.771 --> 00:58:03.274
for those of us that like
to get more "hands on."

839
00:58:03.441 --> 00:58:05.193
ROMAN:
I'm sitting here wondering this whole time.

840
00:58:05.360 --> 00:58:08.279
will this thing fit in valet
at Cheesecake Factory?

841
00:58:08.446 --> 00:58:10.824
No one is getting "hands on."

842
00:58:10.990 --> 00:58:13.284
She doesn't go on city streets.

843
00:58:16.579 --> 00:58:19.708
Wow. I'm in love.

844
00:58:21.876 --> 00:58:23.837
Again. no. no.

845
00:58:24.004 --> 00:58:25.884
That's a million-dollar show car.

846
00:58:25.964 --> 00:58:27.674
The point is to not draw attention.

847
00:58:27.841 --> 00:58:29.843
It's reverse psychology.

848
00:58:29.926 --> 00:58:31.261
Dom would never see it coming.

849
00:58:31.428 --> 00:58:32.721
It's neon orange.

850
00:58:32.887 --> 00:58:35.932
The International Space Station
would see it coming.

851
00:58:36.099 --> 00:58:38.560
Go choose anything less conspicuous.

852
00:58:38.727 --> 00:58:40.395
ROMAN: No. no. no. Calipers are my...

853
00:58:40.562 --> 00:58:41.691
- This is ridiculous.
- Not happening.

854
00:58:41.771 --> 00:58:43.273
Hey. my man.
you can put that down right there.

855
00:58:43.440 --> 00:58:47.152
This is a gift. a real gift.
I know what you're doing.

856
00:58:47.235 --> 00:58:49.279
(LAUGHS) I like your beard.

857
00:58:49.446 --> 00:58:51.239
You're Blanta. Black Santa?

858
00:58:53.116 --> 00:58:55.660
No. I'm serious. Put it down right there.

859
00:59:22.812 --> 00:59:23.938
What are you doing?

860
00:59:24.105 --> 00:59:26.441
<i>Engine's misfiring. I gotta check it out.</i>

861
00:59:26.608 --> 00:59:28.234
No. that's not part of the plan. Dom.

862
00:59:28.401 --> 00:59:29.694
DOM: <i>Clearly.</i>

863
00:59:29.861 --> 00:59:32.405
<i>But unless you want
the engine to seize on the job...</i>

864
00:59:33.490 --> 00:59:34.908
You have five minutes.

865
00:59:42.874 --> 00:59:44.626
(MOUTHING) <i>Five minutes.</i>

866
00:59:47.170 --> 00:59:48.380
I want another visual.

867
00:59:56.721 --> 00:59:57.972
I got an ATM.

868
01:00:09.901 --> 01:00:11.152
I don't like this.

869
01:00:24.958 --> 01:00:26.459
I want to see Toretto.

870
01:00:26.626 --> 01:00:28.420
- There are no more cameras.
- Then find something!

871
01:00:28.586 --> 01:00:29.921
Punch in on something reflective.

872
01:00:30.088 --> 01:00:32.007
A car mirror. anything.

873
01:00:42.100 --> 01:00:43.560
Do you know who I am?

874
01:00:43.727 --> 01:00:45.145
It's why I'm here.

875
01:00:45.895 --> 01:00:48.023
Do you know what I'm capable of?

876
01:00:49.649 --> 01:00:51.484
It's why I'm here.

877
01:00:52.402 --> 01:00:54.863
I'll give you until I finish me cuppa.

878
01:00:55.030 --> 01:00:56.823
And I'm fucking thirsty.

879
01:00:56.990 --> 01:01:00.577
I've got limited time.
so I won't take up too much of yours.

880
01:01:01.369 --> 01:01:02.579
Oh. no.

881
01:01:02.912 --> 01:01:06.207
No. you've already taken everything
I have of value. Mr. Toretto.

882
01:01:06.374 --> 01:01:08.752
What more could you possibly want?

883
01:01:09.627 --> 01:01:11.296
To give you something back.

884
01:01:20.847 --> 01:01:21.931
Talk to me.

885
01:01:25.435 --> 01:01:27.145
Something's not right here.

886
01:01:28.271 --> 01:01:32.776
First time I saw my son
was behind a bulletproof glass.

887
01:01:34.027 --> 01:01:37.572
When he reached for me. I couldn't hold him.

888
01:01:38.990 --> 01:01:40.909
It's the worst pain I ever felt.

889
01:01:42.369 --> 01:01:45.080
I know you know exactly how that feels.

890
01:01:47.040 --> 01:01:49.125
Maybe we could change that.

891
01:01:50.085 --> 01:01:51.586
Now. why do I think

892
01:01:51.753 --> 01:01:56.299
you're about to suggest something
really dodgy. Mr. Toretto?

893
01:02:01.388 --> 01:02:03.348
It's why I'm here.

894
01:02:04.683 --> 01:02:08.186
Jesus. punch in on something.
I'm not liking this. Something's not right.

895
01:02:09.104 --> 01:02:11.481
- Rhodes. you close?
- RHODES: <i>Yeah.</i>

896
01:02:11.898 --> 01:02:12.899
CIPHER: Go.

897
01:02:13.066 --> 01:02:14.776
The delivery truck's moving.

898
01:02:24.994 --> 01:02:26.079
(MOUTHING) <i>I know.</i>

899
01:02:36.965 --> 01:02:38.842
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING OVER RADIO)

900
01:02:47.058 --> 01:02:52.105
HOBBS: "Captain Deckard Shaw
distinguished himself by acts of gallantry

901
01:02:52.272 --> 01:02:55.358
"at the risk of his life above
and beyond the call of duty.

902
01:02:55.775 --> 01:03:00.113
"His bold actions saved the lives
of hostages and his teammates.

903
01:03:00.280 --> 01:03:03.366
"Recommendation: Victoria Cross."

904
01:03:03.742 --> 01:03:06.494
Highest honor the British
government has ever given

905
01:03:08.038 --> 01:03:09.414
to a traitor.

906
01:03:11.374 --> 01:03:13.710
Something about this whole thing
that just doesn't add up to me.

907
01:03:13.877 --> 01:03:15.879
Well. that would be
the same kind of funny math

908
01:03:16.046 --> 01:03:20.342
that says a DSS agent who has
a Silver Star for valor stole an EMP.

909
01:03:20.508 --> 01:03:22.469
Sound familiar. huh?

910
01:03:29.642 --> 01:03:30.643
You want to give me a hand?

911
01:03:34.022 --> 01:03:35.023
- On three?
- Yeah.

912
01:03:35.190 --> 01:03:36.608
One. two. three.

913
01:03:36.691 --> 01:03:37.942
(BOTH GRUNTING)

914
01:03:40.653 --> 01:03:41.654
You know what. Twinkle Toes?

915
01:03:41.821 --> 01:03:44.157
In another life. I bet me and you
could've done some serious damage.

916
01:03:45.450 --> 01:03:46.910
- Yeah. we could've.
- Yeah.

917
01:03:48.453 --> 01:03:51.790
Shame I'm gonna have to bounce your head
off the fender when this is all over.

918
01:03:52.082 --> 01:03:53.625
(MACHINE WHIRRING)

919
01:03:53.917 --> 01:03:56.127
Ah. well. with all due respect. Captain.

920
01:03:56.294 --> 01:03:58.463
when this whole thing is over.
we're gonna find a location.

921
01:03:58.630 --> 01:04:00.382
and I'm gonna knock your teeth
so far down your throat.

922
01:04:00.548 --> 01:04:03.718
you're gonna stick a toothbrush
right up your ass to brush them.

923
01:04:05.929 --> 01:04:07.722
(BOTH LAUGHING)

924
01:04:10.809 --> 01:04:12.018
Give me God's Eye.

925
01:04:12.852 --> 01:04:13.895
God's Eye. active.

926
01:04:14.104 --> 01:04:15.188
Good.

927
01:04:16.189 --> 01:04:17.774
Let's find us a Russian.

928
01:04:18.441 --> 01:04:20.735
I spy with my little eye.

929
01:04:21.152 --> 01:04:23.363
a Minister of Defense.

930
01:04:34.749 --> 01:04:36.459
(SIRENS WAILING)

931
01:04:39.587 --> 01:04:40.755
(MAN SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

932
01:04:40.839 --> 01:04:43.091
We land back in Moscow by nine.

933
01:04:43.258 --> 01:04:45.260
Here's the latest defense report.

934
01:04:45.427 --> 01:04:47.554
All the items in yesterday's brief.

935
01:04:49.806 --> 01:04:51.558
Upload those coordinates to Dom's nav.

936
01:04:51.641 --> 01:04:52.767
Copy that.

937
01:04:59.816 --> 01:05:00.942
(TIRES SQUEALING)

938
01:05:11.286 --> 01:05:12.537
(LAUGHING)

939
01:05:16.041 --> 01:05:17.500
He's in the third car.

940
01:05:18.585 --> 01:05:20.545
(OVER EARPIECE) <i>It's a Guard Class limousine.</i>

941
01:05:24.716 --> 01:05:26.134
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

942
01:05:35.185 --> 01:05:36.227
Where's my team?

943
01:05:36.394 --> 01:05:38.271
- Where's his team?
- There's no sign of them yet.

944
01:05:38.438 --> 01:05:40.023
They're off the grid.

945
01:05:40.106 --> 01:05:42.025
They're probably just
bunkered down somewhere.

946
01:05:42.108 --> 01:05:43.276
DOM: <i>We're closing in on 'em.</i>

947
01:05:45.153 --> 01:05:46.279
You guys ready?

948
01:05:46.446 --> 01:05:50.408
CIPHER: One thing I can guarantee.
Dom. no one's ready for this.

949
01:05:50.867 --> 01:05:53.870
I want every chip with a zero-day
exploit in a two-mile radius

950
01:05:54.037 --> 01:05:55.372
around that motorcade now.

951
01:05:55.538 --> 01:05:56.873
There's over a thousand of them.

952
01:05:57.207 --> 01:05:58.208
Hack 'em all.

953
01:06:10.762 --> 01:06:12.389
(ENGINE STARTS)

954
01:06:15.850 --> 01:06:17.102
It's zombie time.

955
01:06:24.901 --> 01:06:26.653
I'd buckle up if I were you.

956
01:06:28.530 --> 01:06:29.531
- (TIRES SQUEALING)
- Hmm?

957
01:06:30.657 --> 01:06:31.866
WOMAN: (YELLS) What are you doing?

958
01:06:32.575 --> 01:06:33.702
(GRUNTING)

959
01:06:38.790 --> 01:06:39.791
Ah!

960
01:06:40.875 --> 01:06:41.838
(CAR ENGINE STARTING)

961
01:06:41.918 --> 01:06:42.919
(HORNS BLARING)

962
01:07:03.940 --> 01:07:05.275
GOD'S EYE TECH: Safety sensors overridden.

963
01:07:05.358 --> 01:07:06.443
Thank you.

964
01:07:08.778 --> 01:07:09.988
(ENGINE STARTS)

965
01:07:11.656 --> 01:07:12.866
MAN: Whoa.

966
01:07:19.122 --> 01:07:20.790
(TIRES SQUEALING)

967
01:07:21.291 --> 01:07:22.459
(WOMAN SHRIEKING)

968
01:07:22.876 --> 01:07:24.127
(EXCLAIMING)

969
01:07:27.964 --> 01:07:29.215
(YELLS AND GROANS)

970
01:07:29.466 --> 01:07:30.467
Hey!

971
01:07:38.725 --> 01:07:39.809
Target the motorcade.

972
01:07:50.153 --> 01:07:52.155
And here they come.

973
01:07:55.992 --> 01:07:56.993
(IN RUSSIAN)

974
01:07:57.077 --> 01:07:58.161
What is going on?

975
01:07:59.412 --> 01:08:00.413
(IN ENGLISH) Ouch.

976
01:08:02.123 --> 01:08:03.086
- (GRUNTS)
- (IN RUSSIAN)

977
01:08:03.166 --> 01:08:04.167
Drive!

978
01:08:10.090 --> 01:08:11.341
GOD'S EYE TECH: (IN ENGLISH)
Police escort down.

979
01:08:11.716 --> 01:08:13.343
Take out the lead and follow cars.

980
01:08:13.843 --> 01:08:14.886
(ENGINES STARTING)

981
01:08:28.566 --> 01:08:29.567
(IN RUSSIAN)

982
01:08:29.651 --> 01:08:30.652
Drive! Drive!

983
01:08:32.654 --> 01:08:34.197
(BOTH GRUNTING)

984
01:08:40.620 --> 01:08:41.955
- Two more down.
- They're still under warranty.

985
01:08:42.038 --> 01:08:43.039
(RUSSIAN SECRET SERVICE AGENT IN RUSSIAN)

986
01:08:43.123 --> 01:08:44.374
There's more ahead of us.

987
01:08:44.833 --> 01:08:45.834
Shoot their engines!

988
01:08:53.008 --> 01:08:53.970
(ALL SCREAMING)

989
01:08:54.050 --> 01:08:55.051
Oh. God!

990
01:08:58.888 --> 01:08:59.889
(MAN SCREAMING)

991
01:09:09.065 --> 01:09:11.234
OFFICER: (OVER RADIO)
<i>We got an army of cars driving themselves!</i>

992
01:09:11.317 --> 01:09:12.610
<i>Send backup. send SWAT!</i>

993
01:09:12.694 --> 01:09:14.821
<i>I don't care if you send
the goddamn Boy Scouts.</i>

994
01:09:14.904 --> 01:09:16.156
<i>just send 'em some help!</i>

995
01:09:16.239 --> 01:09:17.490
Now. that's Dom.

996
01:09:22.162 --> 01:09:23.163
(IN RUSSIAN)

997
01:09:23.246 --> 01:09:24.247
Faster. faster!

998
01:09:46.353 --> 01:09:47.854
GOD'S EYE TECH:
The motorcade just turned on Seventh.

999
01:09:47.937 --> 01:09:49.522
CIPHER: Perfect. Make it rain.

1000
01:09:49.731 --> 01:09:51.066
(ENGINE STARTS)

1001
01:10:25.809 --> 01:10:26.893
Ah!

1002
01:10:27.102 --> 01:10:28.353
(WOMAN SCREAMS)

1003
01:10:35.610 --> 01:10:36.653
(EXCLAIMS)

1004
01:10:38.405 --> 01:10:39.447
(ALL SCREAMING)

1005
01:10:39.989 --> 01:10:40.990
(IN RUSSIAN)

1006
01:10:41.074 --> 01:10:42.075
Oh. God!

1007
01:10:48.498 --> 01:10:49.499
Target immobilized.

1008
01:10:50.917 --> 01:10:52.043
You're up. Dom.

1009
01:11:05.348 --> 01:11:06.349
(IN RUSSIAN)

1010
01:11:06.433 --> 01:11:07.809
What the hell is that?

1011
01:11:07.976 --> 01:11:09.019
What's he doing?

1012
01:11:12.439 --> 01:11:13.440
What are you waiting for?

1013
01:11:14.274 --> 01:11:15.316
Shoot him!

1014
01:11:15.817 --> 01:11:17.235
Come on. come on!

1015
01:11:26.453 --> 01:11:27.454
I'm out.

1016
01:11:29.247 --> 01:11:30.290
Shit.

1017
01:11:30.373 --> 01:11:31.336
Don't worry. sir.

1018
01:11:31.416 --> 01:11:32.709
The car is impenetrable.

1019
01:11:32.959 --> 01:11:34.044
You'll be safe in here.

1020
01:11:37.380 --> 01:11:38.381
(BOTH GRUNT)

1021
01:11:38.548 --> 01:11:39.758
- DOM: (IN ENGLISH) Give me the case.
- (IN RUSSIAN)

1022
01:11:39.841 --> 01:11:40.804
Give him the case!

1023
01:11:40.884 --> 01:11:42.635
Those are nuclear launch codes.

1024
01:11:42.886 --> 01:11:44.888
We cannot give it to him.

1025
01:11:50.060 --> 01:11:51.061
What is he doing?

1026
01:12:08.536 --> 01:12:09.913
He just cut a hole in our gas tank!

1027
01:12:14.709 --> 01:12:15.710
(TAPPING)

1028
01:12:19.214 --> 01:12:20.423
(PANTING)

1029
01:12:29.474 --> 01:12:31.142
(RUSSIAN SECRET SERVICE AGENT PANTING)

1030
01:12:37.273 --> 01:12:38.608
(IN ENGLISH) Good work. Dom.

1031
01:12:39.567 --> 01:12:40.694
Meet you at the pickup.

1032
01:12:47.784 --> 01:12:48.785
(TIRES SCREECH)

1033
01:12:51.204 --> 01:12:52.831
DOM: <i>I think I know where my team's at.</i>

1034
01:12:53.373 --> 01:12:55.125
- Where?
- Right in front of me.

1035
01:13:08.054 --> 01:13:09.097
This is on you.

1036
01:13:09.848 --> 01:13:11.266
Get out of there. Dom.

1037
01:13:11.558 --> 01:13:13.018
RAMSEY: (OVER RADIO)
<i>Guys. I know why Dom's here.</i>

1038
01:13:13.601 --> 01:13:16.354
Police scanners are saying
he stole a nuclear football.

1039
01:13:19.733 --> 01:13:22.819
(OVER SPEAKERS) <i>It's over. Toretto.
Get your ass outta the car now.</i>

1040
01:13:25.613 --> 01:13:27.240
(ENGINE REVVING)

1041
01:13:29.993 --> 01:13:31.494
<i>So. that's how you wanna play this?</i>

1042
01:13:32.412 --> 01:13:33.663
<i>Let's play.</i>

1043
01:13:39.586 --> 01:13:41.379
Don't do this. Dom.

1044
01:13:44.674 --> 01:13:45.759
He's going for it!

1045
01:13:46.676 --> 01:13:47.969
- What are you doing?
- It's a trap!

1046
01:13:50.722 --> 01:13:51.765
Damn it!

1047
01:13:53.099 --> 01:13:54.100
(WOMAN SCREAMING)

1048
01:14:13.328 --> 01:14:15.872
TEJ: Now I know what it feels like
to be every cop ever chasing us!

1049
01:14:16.039 --> 01:14:17.540
I'm gonna get a little closer.
I'm gonna PIT him.

1050
01:14:17.707 --> 01:14:19.542
Oh. so. you just gonna PIT Dom?

1051
01:14:19.668 --> 01:14:22.671
Little Nobody has clearly
lost his little mind.

1052
01:14:35.225 --> 01:14:36.267
I'm on him.

1053
01:14:36.351 --> 01:14:37.727
Easy. Work together.

1054
01:14:41.523 --> 01:14:42.732
(MEN YELLING)

1055
01:14:47.570 --> 01:14:48.571
Wait. wait. wait!

1056
01:14:50.407 --> 01:14:51.574
Oh. sh...

1057
01:14:58.331 --> 01:14:59.416
I'll take the shortcut!

1058
01:15:03.336 --> 01:15:04.421
(BOTH SCREAMING)

1059
01:15:07.257 --> 01:15:08.800
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

1060
01:15:12.804 --> 01:15:14.723
RAMSEY: Look out! Watch those people!

1061
01:15:15.598 --> 01:15:17.058
Big Sexy comin' through!

1062
01:15:46.796 --> 01:15:48.006
Not this time. Dom.

1063
01:15:59.100 --> 01:16:00.101
(PANTING)

1064
01:16:06.733 --> 01:16:07.734
(GRUNTS)

1065
01:16:19.162 --> 01:16:21.164
Watch the drag or the line will snap!

1066
01:16:26.169 --> 01:16:27.212
(GRUNTING)

1067
01:16:47.357 --> 01:16:49.025
Stretch him out! Hold him!

1068
01:16:52.904 --> 01:16:53.905
(GRUNTS)

1069
01:17:17.387 --> 01:17:19.723
He's gotta have about
2.000 horsepower in that thing.

1070
01:17:20.140 --> 01:17:21.141
Try 3.000!

1071
01:17:25.353 --> 01:17:26.521
Try five.

1072
01:17:34.904 --> 01:17:35.905
Get out of there.

1073
01:17:36.072 --> 01:17:37.115
I'm working on it.

1074
01:17:37.198 --> 01:17:39.075
CIPHER: <i>Stop working on it and do it.</i>

1075
01:17:51.504 --> 01:17:53.298
No. no. no. this my Bentley!

1076
01:18:02.432 --> 01:18:03.475
(YELLING)

1077
01:18:03.933 --> 01:18:05.643
No! No!

1078
01:18:22.202 --> 01:18:23.286
(ALL GRUNTING)

1079
01:18:33.213 --> 01:18:35.215
Get that case and run.

1080
01:18:38.718 --> 01:18:39.928
(GRUNTS)

1081
01:18:47.560 --> 01:18:48.770
Move.

1082
01:18:54.859 --> 01:18:56.820
They thought this was
gonna be a street fight.

1083
01:18:57.195 --> 01:18:58.321
What are you waiting for. Toretto?

1084
01:19:00.323 --> 01:19:01.324
- (GUNSHOTS)
- (PEOPLE SCREAMING)

1085
01:19:01.408 --> 01:19:02.575
No!

1086
01:19:06.329 --> 01:19:08.081
(SIREN WAILING)

1087
01:19:12.502 --> 01:19:13.670
(SIGHS)

1088
01:19:15.380 --> 01:19:16.464
Letty. stop!

1089
01:19:21.511 --> 01:19:22.512
What are you gonna do?

1090
01:19:26.016 --> 01:19:27.225
(GASPS)

1091
01:19:35.692 --> 01:19:39.612
I don't know why you're doing this.
but I know one thing.

1092
01:19:41.156 --> 01:19:42.198
You love me.

1093
01:19:46.870 --> 01:19:48.788
And you are not gonna shoot me.

1094
01:20:00.383 --> 01:20:03.678
You should've given him the case.
'cause I won't chase you.

1095
01:20:05.972 --> 01:20:07.182
Okay.

1096
01:20:07.891 --> 01:20:09.768
I will just take it from a dead girl.

1097
01:20:11.728 --> 01:20:13.229
DOM: You willing to die for it?

1098
01:20:31.581 --> 01:20:32.707
Let's go. then.

1099
01:20:54.437 --> 01:20:55.438
HOBBS: Anything?

1100
01:20:56.439 --> 01:20:57.607
They're gone.

1101
01:20:59.025 --> 01:21:01.111
And DOD confirmed it was a nuclear football.

1102
01:21:01.444 --> 01:21:03.947
He's got an EMP and nuclear launch codes.

1103
01:21:05.407 --> 01:21:08.910
I don't know what it is.
but they're building towards something.

1104
01:21:09.327 --> 01:21:10.412
Deckard?

1105
01:21:11.955 --> 01:21:13.039
LITTLE NOBODY: He didn't make it.

1106
01:21:21.464 --> 01:21:22.465
(GRUNTS)

1107
01:21:34.644 --> 01:21:36.021
CIPHER: (OVER INTERCOM)
<i>I'm disappointed in you. Dom.</i>

1108
01:21:37.063 --> 01:21:40.483
<i>When push came to shove. you were gonna
let Letty just walk away with the codes.</i>

1109
01:21:40.567 --> 01:21:41.693
You got the codes!

1110
01:21:41.776 --> 01:21:43.319
<i>Rhodes got the codes.</i>

1111
01:21:43.903 --> 01:21:46.322
<i>You made the choice to let her go.</i>

1112
01:21:48.158 --> 01:21:50.160
And now I have to make one of my own.

1113
01:21:57.792 --> 01:21:59.669
(MUFFLED SOBBING)

1114
01:22:02.339 --> 01:22:06.009
(WHISPERING) They are adorable
little things. aren't they?

1115
01:22:06.801 --> 01:22:08.595
God. I hope I don't hurt him.

1116
01:22:13.350 --> 01:22:16.019
Look. psychotic. I did exactly
what you asked me to do.

1117
01:22:17.145 --> 01:22:18.271
Don't do this.

1118
01:22:18.646 --> 01:22:20.023
This is your doing.

1119
01:22:20.357 --> 01:22:21.358
My doing?

1120
01:22:26.029 --> 01:22:27.530
BABY TORETTO: (BABBLING) Da-dada.

1121
01:22:27.697 --> 01:22:28.948
Dada.

1122
01:22:29.366 --> 01:22:30.575
Da-da.

1123
01:22:31.159 --> 01:22:32.911
Please don't hurt him. I'm begging you.

1124
01:22:32.994 --> 01:22:35.372
I don't want you to beg.

1125
01:22:37.874 --> 01:22:39.334
I want you to learn.

1126
01:22:39.709 --> 01:22:41.044
Learn what?

1127
01:22:42.337 --> 01:22:46.007
I understand why you did
what you did. I really do.

1128
01:22:48.677 --> 01:22:49.803
Da-da.

1129
01:22:52.555 --> 01:22:54.516
But it was the wrong choice.

1130
01:22:55.392 --> 01:22:57.894
This is the consequence of that.

1131
01:22:59.646 --> 01:23:00.647
(MUFFLED SCREAMING) No!

1132
01:23:00.814 --> 01:23:02.565
No! No!

1133
01:23:02.732 --> 01:23:03.983
Wait. wait. wait. Wait.

1134
01:23:05.318 --> 01:23:06.945
Save your son!

1135
01:23:07.362 --> 01:23:08.405
No!

1136
01:23:08.697 --> 01:23:09.698
(GUNSHOTS)

1137
01:23:10.031 --> 01:23:11.449
(CRYING)

1138
01:23:18.123 --> 01:23:19.416
(SHUSHING)

1139
01:23:33.763 --> 01:23:34.889
(EXHALES)

1140
01:23:35.598 --> 01:23:38.101
Can you pull up the footage
from the guy in the alley?

1141
01:23:38.810 --> 01:23:39.894
Traffic cams.

1142
01:23:40.061 --> 01:23:41.062
I got you.

1143
01:23:45.608 --> 01:23:46.651
I knew it.

1144
01:23:47.110 --> 01:23:48.403
I recognize that guy.

1145
01:23:49.362 --> 01:23:50.613
That's Connor Rhodes.

1146
01:23:51.031 --> 01:23:53.700
I met him when I was working
with Shaw's brother.

1147
01:23:53.783 --> 01:23:56.077
He wanted us to get
the Nightshade device for him.

1148
01:23:56.494 --> 01:23:57.704
Connor Rhodes.

1149
01:23:58.538 --> 01:24:00.919
He's also linked to somebody
I'd quite like to forget.

1150
01:24:00.999 --> 01:24:02.500
It's Mose Jakande.

1151
01:24:03.209 --> 01:24:05.170
Warlord who tried to get God's Eye.

1152
01:24:05.253 --> 01:24:07.922
Which means that's twice that Dom
has messed up Cipher's business.

1153
01:24:21.728 --> 01:24:26.232
Everything you're feeling right now.
this rage. a sense of loss. it's not real.

1154
01:24:27.734 --> 01:24:31.571
It's a survival instinct
wired deep into our brains

1155
01:24:31.654 --> 01:24:34.324
to ensure continuation of the species.

1156
01:24:35.533 --> 01:24:38.995
When early man would visit a watering hole.

1157
01:24:39.079 --> 01:24:40.997
if they didn't watch their child.

1158
01:24:41.081 --> 01:24:43.500
and it got snatched by a crocodile.

1159
01:24:44.542 --> 01:24:50.548
our brains would create
a painful but instructional memory.

1160
01:24:52.008 --> 01:24:53.760
so it would never happen again.

1161
01:24:56.012 --> 01:24:59.099
This idea of "family"
that is so core with you.

1162
01:24:59.265 --> 01:25:01.017
that rules your world.

1163
01:25:03.019 --> 01:25:04.604
it's a biological lie.

1164
01:25:06.356 --> 01:25:08.066
You don't have to accept it.

1165
01:25:10.527 --> 01:25:11.569
I don't.

1166
01:25:14.531 --> 01:25:17.534
Did you really think you
could destroy two of my teams

1167
01:25:17.617 --> 01:25:19.369
without any repercussions?

1168
01:25:20.578 --> 01:25:23.373
I wouldn't have even looked
your way if you hadn't done that.

1169
01:25:23.998 --> 01:25:26.001
You didn't even know you had a kid.

1170
01:25:27.419 --> 01:25:30.922
You can thank me for that and start
doing the job I'm asking you to do.

1171
01:25:31.089 --> 01:25:32.507
Help you start a war.

1172
01:25:32.674 --> 01:25:34.509
Is that what you think I want?

1173
01:25:37.220 --> 01:25:38.471
That's so limited.

1174
01:25:40.223 --> 01:25:42.100
I didn't take that football to start a war

1175
01:25:42.183 --> 01:25:44.894
any more than I took
your son to start a family.

1176
01:25:45.854 --> 01:25:47.731
Taking your son got me the codes.

1177
01:25:48.189 --> 01:25:50.362
The codes will get me the nukes

1178
01:25:50.442 --> 01:25:52.819
and the nukes will get me what I want

1179
01:25:52.902 --> 01:25:57.407
today. tomorrow. and every day after that.

1180
01:25:57.615 --> 01:25:59.075
And what's that?

1181
01:26:01.244 --> 01:26:02.495
Accountability.

1182
01:26:04.956 --> 01:26:07.167
The second I fire off one of those nukes.

1183
01:26:07.250 --> 01:26:10.628
I put the superpowers
of this world on notice that.

1184
01:26:10.712 --> 01:26:12.255
when they cross the line.

1185
01:26:14.758 --> 01:26:17.260
I'm gonna be there to hold them responsible.

1186
01:26:19.095 --> 01:26:21.056
Because the truth is. Dom.

1187
01:26:21.598 --> 01:26:23.141
to the world out there.

1188
01:26:26.102 --> 01:26:28.688
I am the crocodile at the watering hole.

1189
01:26:35.153 --> 01:26:36.988
We've got one last job to do.

1190
01:26:38.865 --> 01:26:40.116
DOM: Cipher.

1191
01:26:49.584 --> 01:26:50.960
If I were you. I'd kiss my son.

1192
01:26:54.881 --> 01:26:58.593
Because whether
you value it or not. all of this.

1193
01:26:59.386 --> 01:27:02.764
your plane. your security. and you.

1194
01:27:03.765 --> 01:27:05.809
are still on this earth because of him.

1195
01:27:11.648 --> 01:27:14.404
RAMSEY: <i>The problem we've had with
tracking Cipher is there's nothing to trace.</i>

1196
01:27:14.484 --> 01:27:15.947
But now. we have Rhodes' information.

1197
01:27:16.027 --> 01:27:19.698
And we're getting snapshots of his data
before it's scrubbed off the net.

1198
01:27:19.781 --> 01:27:22.454
That looks like somebody's bank account.
so why don't we just go ahead...

1199
01:27:22.534 --> 01:27:23.702
It's a longitude.

1200
01:27:24.411 --> 01:27:26.663
Given the fact that Dom
hit a Russian motorcade.

1201
01:27:26.746 --> 01:27:28.998
it's safe to say it's Russia.
Go ahead and bring up the map.

1202
01:27:30.291 --> 01:27:32.252
Good. Let's start here
and run the possibilities.

1203
01:27:33.003 --> 01:27:35.672
Yalta. Poltava...

1204
01:27:35.755 --> 01:27:37.173
It's like they just threw letters together.

1205
01:27:37.507 --> 01:27:38.550
Kronyurt.

1206
01:27:38.633 --> 01:27:39.843
MR. NOBODY: It's "Vladovin."

1207
01:27:40.051 --> 01:27:41.594
- What are you doing here?
- What?

1208
01:27:41.761 --> 01:27:44.643
Told you I was gonna check in on you from
time to time to see how you were doin'.

1209
01:27:44.723 --> 01:27:46.182
By the way. not so hot.

1210
01:27:46.808 --> 01:27:49.394
But there's nothing in Vladovin.
It's just ice.

1211
01:27:49.477 --> 01:27:50.645
That's funny.

1212
01:27:50.937 --> 01:27:52.856
Could've sworn there was
a secret Russian naval base

1213
01:27:52.939 --> 01:27:54.858
where they retrofitted Cold War submarines.

1214
01:27:54.941 --> 01:27:57.235
Well. technically. it's not Russian anymore.

1215
01:27:57.861 --> 01:27:58.862
The base was taken over

1216
01:27:58.945 --> 01:28:01.239
by a terror group of military
separatists about a month ago.

1217
01:28:01.322 --> 01:28:02.953
and the Russians haven't taken it back yet.

1218
01:28:03.033 --> 01:28:05.285
so there is a little window
of opportunity here.

1219
01:28:05.535 --> 01:28:07.871
Russian submarines. Nuclear football.

1220
01:28:08.038 --> 01:28:11.249
It sounds like everything we do.
our legs gonna be blown off.

1221
01:28:11.416 --> 01:28:14.669
It sounds like you still
number 11 on the list. (CHUCKLES)

1222
01:28:15.211 --> 01:28:16.755
It sounds like you've changed

1223
01:28:16.838 --> 01:28:19.257
since your little punk-ass
facial hairs done came in.

1224
01:28:19.382 --> 01:28:20.467
Guys. guys.

1225
01:28:20.550 --> 01:28:22.886
Hey. we gotta call this in.
All the way up the chain.

1226
01:28:22.969 --> 01:28:25.764
That's good thinking. champ.
except unfortunately.

1227
01:28:25.847 --> 01:28:27.891
the Russian Minister of Defense

1228
01:28:27.974 --> 01:28:30.727
got himself involved in a little
incident on US territory.

1229
01:28:30.810 --> 01:28:32.937
and the two governments aren't talking
to each other for a while.

1230
01:28:33.021 --> 01:28:34.647
By the time they do. it'll be too late.

1231
01:28:34.731 --> 01:28:36.524
So. any other suggestions?

1232
01:28:37.359 --> 01:28:39.402
HOBBS: Yeah. I got one.

1233
01:28:40.278 --> 01:28:42.113
How about we just stop them ourselves?

1234
01:28:42.197 --> 01:28:44.074
You're talking about a Russian military base.

1235
01:28:44.157 --> 01:28:45.325
Separatist.

1236
01:28:45.408 --> 01:28:46.493
Whatever. It's suicide.

1237
01:28:46.576 --> 01:28:48.036
It's stopping World War III.

1238
01:28:50.163 --> 01:28:51.247
What's it gonna be. rook?

1239
01:28:51.748 --> 01:28:53.833
You gonna close your eyes on this one. too?

1240
01:28:54.000 --> 01:28:56.961
Pray that the apocalypse doesn't come
knocking on your mama's front door?

1241
01:28:57.671 --> 01:29:00.006
Or. are you gonna saddle up. be a man.

1242
01:29:00.090 --> 01:29:02.592
and save the entire goddamn world?

1243
01:29:08.598 --> 01:29:11.059
You know. I think I figured it out.

1244
01:29:11.351 --> 01:29:12.477
What's that?

1245
01:29:12.644 --> 01:29:14.521
- Rule number three.
- Which is?

1246
01:29:16.022 --> 01:29:17.107
There are no rules.

1247
01:29:18.358 --> 01:29:19.404
(MR. NOBODY LAUGHS)

1248
01:29:19.484 --> 01:29:22.612
What'd I tell you. Luke?
I knew he'd get it in three.

1249
01:29:22.779 --> 01:29:24.322
LITTLE NOBODY:
Aerial transport leaves in an hour.

1250
01:29:24.406 --> 01:29:26.950
Take whatever vehicle you want.
All bets are off.

1251
01:29:27.158 --> 01:29:28.868
- All bets are off?
- Bets are off?

1252
01:29:28.952 --> 01:29:30.286
<i>Do svidanya!</i>

1253
01:29:56.146 --> 01:29:57.814
Letty. I don't like telling you this one bit.

1254
01:29:58.314 --> 01:29:59.774
But the game's changed.

1255
01:30:00.316 --> 01:30:03.153
Before. we were just trying to catch Dom.
but now. after all this.

1256
01:30:03.403 --> 01:30:05.155
I want you to know. if I have to.

1257
01:30:06.656 --> 01:30:07.782
I'm gonna put him down.

1258
01:30:10.827 --> 01:30:12.412
Then you might have to take us both down.

1259
01:30:14.164 --> 01:30:15.457
ROMAN: I'm freezing. man.

1260
01:30:15.915 --> 01:30:17.208
(BREATHING HEAVILY) This ain't for me.

1261
01:30:17.667 --> 01:30:20.211
I come from a different
kind of lifestyle. brah.

1262
01:30:22.380 --> 01:30:25.842
Ladies know me.
They know where I'm at with it.

1263
01:30:27.052 --> 01:30:31.014
I tried to take a piss.
I didn't even recognize myself.

1264
01:30:31.431 --> 01:30:33.683
Man. that's entirely too much information.

1265
01:30:33.850 --> 01:30:34.934
I'm just sayin'.

1266
01:30:35.101 --> 01:30:36.770
Well. one thing's for sure.

1267
01:30:37.687 --> 01:30:40.151
Dom's gotta be either working
with them or making a trade.

1268
01:30:40.231 --> 01:30:41.691
because no one would be this insane

1269
01:30:41.775 --> 01:30:43.360
to hit this place without a damn army.

1270
01:30:44.527 --> 01:30:46.696
I wouldn't be so sure about that.

1271
01:30:48.156 --> 01:30:49.366
HOBBS: Speak of the devil.

1272
01:30:57.374 --> 01:31:00.710
All right. Dom. you're one step
closer to that family reunion.

1273
01:31:00.877 --> 01:31:02.045
400 meters to base.

1274
01:31:02.212 --> 01:31:04.547
Prep the EMP. Let's take these defenses down.

1275
01:31:13.098 --> 01:31:14.391
(ENGINE REVVING)

1276
01:31:15.225 --> 01:31:16.226
(MAN SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

1277
01:31:16.309 --> 01:31:17.560
We have a possible threat approaching.

1278
01:31:18.186 --> 01:31:21.606
Raise the barricade.

1279
01:31:38.081 --> 01:31:40.083
We've lost power. defensive positions now.

1280
01:31:42.127 --> 01:31:44.921
(CLAPS) (IN ENGLISH) Gates are open.
Let's get this party started.

1281
01:31:50.051 --> 01:31:51.428
(SOLDIERS YELLING IN RUSSIAN)

1282
01:32:00.937 --> 01:32:02.564
- EMP is recharging.
- How long?

1283
01:32:02.897 --> 01:32:04.107
Sixty seconds.

1284
01:32:04.983 --> 01:32:07.527
All right. Dom. you have
one pulse left in that EMP.

1285
01:32:08.028 --> 01:32:09.654
That sub is heavily insulated.

1286
01:32:09.821 --> 01:32:11.990
You're gonna need to be right
underneath it for this thing to work.

1287
01:32:14.159 --> 01:32:15.452
(TIRES SQUEALING)

1288
01:32:32.302 --> 01:32:33.303
(GRUNTING)

1289
01:32:36.348 --> 01:32:37.807
- Come on.
- (SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

1290
01:32:37.891 --> 01:32:39.893
Engaging target. He's beneath the sub.

1291
01:32:44.856 --> 01:32:45.982
(ALARMS BLARING)

1292
01:32:46.107 --> 01:32:48.568
Mayday! Mayday! I've lost all power.
I'm going down.

1293
01:32:55.325 --> 01:32:56.326
CIPHER: <i>Yes!</i>

1294
01:32:56.493 --> 01:32:57.994
Two birds with one stone.

1295
01:32:58.161 --> 01:32:59.496
SUPER JET TECH: We've got control of the sub.

1296
01:32:59.579 --> 01:33:02.248
Dom. we are good.
Head over to the rendezvous.

1297
01:33:02.332 --> 01:33:05.418
Okay. Matty. let's take this baby for a spin.

1298
01:33:11.091 --> 01:33:12.258
TEJ: Damn!

1299
01:33:12.425 --> 01:33:15.011
I think Cipher just rebooted that
sub to slave its command system.

1300
01:33:15.345 --> 01:33:16.721
What the hell is he talking about?

1301
01:33:16.971 --> 01:33:20.517
In layman's terms.
she just carjacked a submarine.

1302
01:33:22.060 --> 01:33:23.645
We can't let it get away.

1303
01:33:24.396 --> 01:33:25.730
There's the control room.

1304
01:33:26.314 --> 01:33:28.233
If you can get me into that wheelhouse.

1305
01:33:28.316 --> 01:33:30.280
I can tap the network
and counter-hack Cipher.

1306
01:33:30.360 --> 01:33:31.990
Keep it from lowering into the water.

1307
01:33:32.070 --> 01:33:33.947
No. what we need to do is get me on that sub.

1308
01:33:34.197 --> 01:33:36.199
I find the weapons room
and I can pull the launch chip

1309
01:33:36.282 --> 01:33:37.701
before she can fire any of those nukes.

1310
01:33:37.867 --> 01:33:38.952
That is too crazy.

1311
01:33:39.119 --> 01:33:40.412
What you're saying is too dangerous.

1312
01:33:40.495 --> 01:33:41.538
We'll do both.

1313
01:34:05.937 --> 01:34:06.938
Knock. knock.

1314
01:34:09.357 --> 01:34:10.650
(SOLDIERS YELLING IN RUSSIAN)

1315
01:34:12.027 --> 01:34:14.320
(IN ENGLISH)
Five vehicles just breached the base.

1316
01:34:14.487 --> 01:34:16.156
They just don't give up. do they?

1317
01:34:25.206 --> 01:34:27.792
HOBBS: All right. let's haul ass. team.
Double time. double time!

1318
01:34:28.251 --> 01:34:29.753
(SOLDIERS YELLING IN RUSSIAN)

1319
01:34:32.881 --> 01:34:33.882
(YELLING)

1320
01:34:35.467 --> 01:34:36.843
Letty. let's roll!

1321
01:34:38.136 --> 01:34:39.137
(GROANS)

1322
01:34:39.220 --> 01:34:40.638
Go! Go. go. go!

1323
01:35:16.883 --> 01:35:17.926
CIPHER: <i>Change of plans. Dom.</i>

1324
01:35:18.218 --> 01:35:20.303
I'm sending you new coordinates.
Head there immediately.

1325
01:35:20.679 --> 01:35:22.222
<i>I'm done. I want my son.</i>

1326
01:35:22.305 --> 01:35:23.473
I'll tell you when you're done.

1327
01:35:23.848 --> 01:35:25.183
<i>Your team is in play.</i>

1328
01:35:25.266 --> 01:35:27.644
Now. meet Rhodes and follow my instruction.

1329
01:35:31.981 --> 01:35:32.982
(PANTING)

1330
01:35:33.066 --> 01:35:34.693
I've got you covered! Go!

1331
01:35:37.654 --> 01:35:40.156
Move. move! Get outta here! Go. go. go!

1332
01:35:43.910 --> 01:35:45.662
(PANTING)

1333
01:35:48.081 --> 01:35:50.166
Okay. How do you like this?

1334
01:35:50.667 --> 01:35:52.502
(ENGINE POWERING DOWN)

1335
01:35:53.461 --> 01:35:56.047
- JET TECH: Remote link has been severed.
- CIPHER: I'll take care of this.

1336
01:35:59.968 --> 01:36:01.302
Hi. Ramsey.

1337
01:36:03.263 --> 01:36:04.931
(ENGINE POWERING UP)

1338
01:36:05.181 --> 01:36:06.433
RAMSEY: She's regained control.

1339
01:36:06.599 --> 01:36:07.851
Damn it. She's good.

1340
01:36:08.476 --> 01:36:09.477
(DOOR UNLOCKING)

1341
01:36:16.151 --> 01:36:17.527
(BOTH GRUNTING)

1342
01:36:26.828 --> 01:36:27.829
(YELLS)

1343
01:36:34.836 --> 01:36:35.837
(ALL GRUNTING)

1344
01:36:45.138 --> 01:36:46.556
(PANTING)

1345
01:36:49.267 --> 01:36:50.480
TECH: They're entering the weapons room.

1346
01:36:50.560 --> 01:36:51.603
Oh. that's cute.

1347
01:36:58.234 --> 01:36:59.361
LITTLE NOBODY: (EXCLAIMS) Pull! Pull!

1348
01:36:59.736 --> 01:37:02.072
Roman. Roman! We gotta find the chip. go!

1349
01:37:05.617 --> 01:37:06.826
Oh. she's slick.

1350
01:37:07.077 --> 01:37:08.578
Gonna have to do better than that. though.

1351
01:37:10.663 --> 01:37:12.582
Okay. now you're starting to piss me off.

1352
01:37:13.333 --> 01:37:14.334
(GRUNTING)

1353
01:37:24.928 --> 01:37:25.929
(MAN YELLING)

1354
01:37:27.806 --> 01:37:29.891
Ramsey. how much time we talkin' here?

1355
01:37:30.350 --> 01:37:33.395
You're smart. but not smart enough.

1356
01:37:34.312 --> 01:37:35.730
(ENGINE POWERING UP)

1357
01:37:36.898 --> 01:37:37.899
She's locked me out.

1358
01:37:40.110 --> 01:37:41.319
(GRUNTING)

1359
01:37:41.945 --> 01:37:44.367
Tej. I can't stop her.
You're gonna have to pull that chip.

1360
01:37:44.447 --> 01:37:46.578
I can't! This thing's gone into attack mode!

1361
01:37:46.658 --> 01:37:48.785
<i>The door's not gonna open
until you pull the chip!</i>

1362
01:37:49.828 --> 01:37:52.622
Tej. we got no idea
what the hell we're looking for.

1363
01:37:53.998 --> 01:37:55.000
I got it!

1364
01:37:56.292 --> 01:37:57.627
(ALARM BLARING)

1365
01:37:57.961 --> 01:38:00.422
What in the hell are you guys doin'?

1366
01:38:01.423 --> 01:38:03.466
It wasn't me. It wasn't me. okay?

1367
01:38:03.550 --> 01:38:05.135
It'll be labeled "Guidance Go."

1368
01:38:05.343 --> 01:38:07.178
- Guidance Go. Guidance Go...
- Okay. I got somethin'.

1369
01:38:07.262 --> 01:38:08.638
- What?
- It says...

1370
01:38:10.306 --> 01:38:12.767
(SPEAKING GIBBERISH)

1371
01:38:14.769 --> 01:38:15.895
Do you understand that?

1372
01:38:21.067 --> 01:38:22.318
(GROANING)

1373
01:38:24.487 --> 01:38:25.989
(MAN LAUGHING)

1374
01:38:30.827 --> 01:38:31.828
(GROANING)

1375
01:38:33.538 --> 01:38:35.415
- (YELLING)
- (SPLATTERING)

1376
01:38:36.458 --> 01:38:38.001
(PANTING)

1377
01:38:40.920 --> 01:38:42.380
Wow. Nasty.

1378
01:38:53.725 --> 01:38:54.768
Hmm.

1379
01:38:56.019 --> 01:38:57.354
Quite a show.

1380
01:39:00.440 --> 01:39:01.441
We're arming the nuke.

1381
01:39:04.402 --> 01:39:06.071
(POWERING UP)

1382
01:39:06.821 --> 01:39:09.282
TEJ: (OVER RADIO) <i>Nuke's going hot!
She's tryin' to fire this thing!</i>

1383
01:39:09.366 --> 01:39:11.496
Roger that. We're moving out.
(OVER RADIO) Disable the nukes!

1384
01:39:11.576 --> 01:39:13.203
Roman. what are you seeing?
Come on. talk to me.

1385
01:39:13.328 --> 01:39:14.954
I don't see shit. I'm holding on!

1386
01:39:15.246 --> 01:39:16.247
(RUMBLING)

1387
01:39:16.831 --> 01:39:18.083
And we have a countdown.

1388
01:39:20.543 --> 01:39:21.628
(ALARM BLARING)

1389
01:39:21.711 --> 01:39:23.421
What the hell is goin' on. man?

1390
01:39:23.505 --> 01:39:26.549
<i>We're about to launch a nuclear missile.
is what the hell is goin' on!</i>

1391
01:39:26.633 --> 01:39:27.676
<i>Pull the damn chip!</i>

1392
01:39:28.593 --> 01:39:29.803
(PANTING)

1393
01:39:31.096 --> 01:39:33.473
Countdown. countdown! Look for a countdown!

1394
01:39:33.556 --> 01:39:34.599
What countdown?

1395
01:39:34.683 --> 01:39:36.309
The missiles need to activate to launch.

1396
01:39:36.393 --> 01:39:38.061
The countdown timer won't be in Russian.

1397
01:39:38.353 --> 01:39:39.354
The countdown...

1398
01:39:39.896 --> 01:39:42.065
Let's show the world what we've got.

1399
01:39:43.650 --> 01:39:44.901
ROMAN: No. no. no! Don't press that!

1400
01:39:47.404 --> 01:39:48.405
I got it.

1401
01:39:50.573 --> 01:39:52.409
Something's wrong. It won't launch.

1402
01:39:54.119 --> 01:39:56.621
Get that sub outta there. Now!

1403
01:39:59.207 --> 01:40:00.750
LITTLE NOBODY: Move your ass. Roman!

1404
01:40:00.834 --> 01:40:02.210
(PANTING)

1405
01:40:08.717 --> 01:40:09.801
You all right?

1406
01:40:09.884 --> 01:40:11.428
There's nothing all right about any of this!

1407
01:40:11.886 --> 01:40:13.805
- Let's go!
- What about the missiles?

1408
01:40:15.056 --> 01:40:17.062
We got the chip. No nukes for her.

1409
01:40:17.142 --> 01:40:19.269
Hell. yeah. Let's roll.

1410
01:40:23.398 --> 01:40:25.942
Guys. we got company. A lot of company!

1411
01:40:30.864 --> 01:40:32.032
All right. team. here's the plan.

1412
01:40:32.198 --> 01:40:33.950
There's a sea lock at the opening of the bay.

1413
01:40:34.159 --> 01:40:35.285
<i>We get there first and close it.</i>

1414
01:40:35.368 --> 01:40:38.288
we can stop the submarine
from escaping into open water

1415
01:40:38.413 --> 01:40:39.831
<i>and disappearing forever.</i>

1416
01:40:41.708 --> 01:40:44.461
I've got the location.
It's 10 miles southwest.

1417
01:40:44.711 --> 01:40:47.172
Ten miles?
We're not gonna make it ten seconds!

1418
01:40:49.341 --> 01:40:51.051
(GUNFIRE)

1419
01:40:53.553 --> 01:40:54.554
Ah!

1420
01:40:54.679 --> 01:40:57.140
No. no. no! This is not good!

1421
01:40:57.974 --> 01:41:00.393
What's the matter. Roman?
Forgot your snow tires?

1422
01:41:00.685 --> 01:41:02.103
ROMAN: Whoa!

1423
01:41:02.312 --> 01:41:03.897
You lovin' that Lambo now?

1424
01:41:04.272 --> 01:41:06.107
ROMAN: Whoa! Ah!

1425
01:41:08.443 --> 01:41:09.486
(ROMAN EXCLAIMS)

1426
01:41:09.986 --> 01:41:10.987
(SCREAMING)

1427
01:41:13.990 --> 01:41:15.325
CIPHER: All right. everyone.

1428
01:41:15.408 --> 01:41:16.659
We'll deal with that launch chip later.

1429
01:41:16.743 --> 01:41:19.457
Right now. I want that sub
in deep water where no one can find it.

1430
01:41:19.537 --> 01:41:21.164
Find me the fastest route out of that bay.

1431
01:41:21.247 --> 01:41:22.248
Copy that.

1432
01:41:31.925 --> 01:41:33.343
Why are they shootin' at me?

1433
01:41:33.426 --> 01:41:35.640
Maybe 'cause you're in an orange
Lamborghini. I don't know.

1434
01:41:35.720 --> 01:41:37.514
Shut up. Tej!

1435
01:41:42.852 --> 01:41:44.187
Dom...

1436
01:41:44.270 --> 01:41:46.022
(OVER EARPIECE)
<i>Do you really wanna put that car in gear?</i>

1437
01:41:47.607 --> 01:41:48.608
Do it.

1438
01:41:48.983 --> 01:41:49.984
Huh?

1439
01:41:52.696 --> 01:41:54.117
I didn't think so.

1440
01:41:54.197 --> 01:41:55.493
They're heading for the sea lock.

1441
01:41:55.573 --> 01:41:56.828
They're trying to trap the sub in the bay.

1442
01:41:56.908 --> 01:41:59.831
I should have taken care
of this a long time ago.

1443
01:41:59.911 --> 01:42:02.372
<i>Rhodes. take his team out.</i>

1444
01:42:03.206 --> 01:42:04.416
I'm on it.

1445
01:42:10.130 --> 01:42:11.381
Roman. get in front of me!

1446
01:42:18.221 --> 01:42:19.931
Okay. y'all wanna play rough?

1447
01:42:20.807 --> 01:42:21.808
Now it's my turn.

1448
01:42:36.656 --> 01:42:37.994
Yeah. baby! (LAUGHS)

1449
01:42:38.074 --> 01:42:39.492
(LAUGHS)

1450
01:42:47.083 --> 01:42:49.377
Guys. we got snowmobiles on the right.

1451
01:42:51.546 --> 01:42:52.922
They're gonna flank us!

1452
01:42:57.093 --> 01:42:58.094
No. they ain't!

1453
01:43:04.100 --> 01:43:05.310
Oh. shit!

1454
01:43:09.439 --> 01:43:10.482
(BEEPING)

1455
01:43:19.699 --> 01:43:20.700
Tej!

1456
01:43:20.825 --> 01:43:22.577
Roman. hold tight. I'm on the way!

1457
01:43:27.082 --> 01:43:29.167
I don't wanna go swimmin'! No!

1458
01:43:35.256 --> 01:43:36.466
Really. Tej?

1459
01:43:39.969 --> 01:43:41.346
Oh. no. no. no!

1460
01:43:45.350 --> 01:43:46.434
Oh. shit!

1461
01:43:49.187 --> 01:43:50.400
Roman. grab your door!

1462
01:43:50.480 --> 01:43:51.564
ROMAN: <i>Tej!</i>

1463
01:43:51.815 --> 01:43:53.111
TEJ: <i>Grab the door. Roman!</i>

1464
01:43:53.191 --> 01:43:54.192
- ROMAN: <i>It's so cold!</i>
- Shit!

1465
01:43:54.818 --> 01:43:55.819
<i>Oh. shit!</i>

1466
01:44:02.617 --> 01:44:03.827
ROMAN: Whoa!

1467
01:44:04.244 --> 01:44:05.453
- Whoo!
- Yeah!

1468
01:44:06.162 --> 01:44:07.792
What is going on?

1469
01:44:07.872 --> 01:44:08.957
Roman. hang on!

1470
01:44:10.500 --> 01:44:11.501
Tej!

1471
01:44:15.213 --> 01:44:16.798
Get me off of this thing!

1472
01:44:17.173 --> 01:44:18.508
Tej!

1473
01:44:22.012 --> 01:44:23.013
Come on!

1474
01:44:32.897 --> 01:44:34.274
Argh!

1475
01:44:38.028 --> 01:44:40.363
All right. I've had enough of this shit!

1476
01:44:40.905 --> 01:44:42.282
(GRUNTS AND GROANS)

1477
01:44:44.576 --> 01:44:46.870
(ALL GROANING)

1478
01:44:54.586 --> 01:44:56.212
Number 11. my ass!

1479
01:44:58.882 --> 01:45:01.551
Yo. shrinkage! We got a sub to catch. Get in!

1480
01:45:15.398 --> 01:45:16.399
What?

1481
01:45:16.483 --> 01:45:17.734
Depressurization alert in the cargo hold.

1482
01:45:17.942 --> 01:45:19.569
Drop it to 10.000 feet.

1483
01:45:20.403 --> 01:45:22.781
I know how much these people mean to you.

1484
01:45:22.864 --> 01:45:24.949
So I will let you pick the first target.

1485
01:45:25.033 --> 01:45:26.743
I don't pick a target from a mile away.

1486
01:45:28.578 --> 01:45:31.081
I stand face to face
and look 'em dead in the eye.

1487
01:45:31.790 --> 01:45:32.916
(CHUCKLES)

1488
01:45:33.249 --> 01:45:34.626
Okay.

1489
01:45:34.709 --> 01:45:35.919
The wife it is.

1490
01:45:43.551 --> 01:45:44.761
(BOTH GRUNTING)

1491
01:45:54.062 --> 01:45:57.023
Nice plane. I'm gonna enjoy having this.

1492
01:45:57.816 --> 01:45:59.150
Hey. don't go gettin' any ideas.

1493
01:45:59.234 --> 01:46:00.819
You and planes don't have a good history.

1494
01:46:03.321 --> 01:46:04.823
No shit.

1495
01:46:04.906 --> 01:46:07.617
Okay. let's go. Scarface.

1496
01:46:08.284 --> 01:46:09.786
These assholes ain't gonna kill themselves.

1497
01:46:13.498 --> 01:46:15.291
Pull up surveillance right now.

1498
01:46:16.876 --> 01:46:18.169
(COMPUTER TRILLS)

1499
01:46:20.422 --> 01:46:21.798
<i>Surprise.</i>

1500
01:46:23.425 --> 01:46:25.427
You're supposed to be dead.

1501
01:46:34.644 --> 01:46:35.645
(IN SPANISH)

1502
01:46:35.770 --> 01:46:36.733
You're driving.

1503
01:46:36.813 --> 01:46:38.276
- I said from the beginning...
- No way.

1504
01:46:38.356 --> 01:46:39.983
- I am not going to drive.
- I'm not driving.

1505
01:46:41.651 --> 01:46:45.155
We have a security breach in
the cargo hold. Take care of it now.

1506
01:46:47.615 --> 01:46:48.616
(GASPS)

1507
01:46:50.660 --> 01:46:53.580
Jesus. Mum.
You're supposed to avoid the nerves.

1508
01:46:53.663 --> 01:46:55.165
Oh. shut up. Don't be such a baby.

1509
01:47:01.588 --> 01:47:02.589
Get to the pilot.

1510
01:47:02.672 --> 01:47:04.341
He's got the second key. Wait for my signal.

1511
01:47:05.008 --> 01:47:06.343
Give Cipher my regards.

1512
01:47:07.469 --> 01:47:09.179
Did Toretto hold up his end of the deal?

1513
01:47:20.899 --> 01:47:23.068
MRS. SHAW: <i>He gave us this little thing here.</i>

1514
01:47:23.360 --> 01:47:25.362
No. no. no. Don't touch.

1515
01:47:25.987 --> 01:47:27.238
You can track Cipher with this.

1516
01:47:27.322 --> 01:47:30.287
but you can't do this on your own.
There's gotta be two of ya.

1517
01:47:30.367 --> 01:47:32.369
Fine. I've got contacts.

1518
01:47:33.495 --> 01:47:34.954
No. you're gonna take your brother.

1519
01:47:35.038 --> 01:47:36.247
- Oh. dear...
- Yes.

1520
01:47:37.123 --> 01:47:39.292
(ALL GRUNTING)

1521
01:47:40.377 --> 01:47:42.420
Toretto knows where he is.

1522
01:47:42.504 --> 01:47:44.089
He's got this thing. It can see everything.

1523
01:47:44.172 --> 01:47:46.549
It's like... It's called
the Devil's Bum Hole or something.

1524
01:47:46.633 --> 01:47:47.717
It's called the God's Eye.

1525
01:47:47.801 --> 01:47:48.885
Yeah. well. whatever.

1526
01:47:49.719 --> 01:47:51.262
(GRUNTING)

1527
01:47:51.388 --> 01:47:53.977
There's no way I'm using Owen. all right?

1528
01:47:54.057 --> 01:47:55.767
He's a lost cause.

1529
01:47:55.850 --> 01:47:58.895
He's your brother. Decks. He's my son.

1530
01:47:59.396 --> 01:48:00.855
He's our family.

1531
01:48:01.731 --> 01:48:04.984
And our family don't die in bloody cages.
(CRYING)

1532
01:48:05.360 --> 01:48:08.488
How can you talk like that about Owen?
I can't believe you.

1533
01:48:08.571 --> 01:48:11.661
You've gone and upset me.
You've really upset your mother.

1534
01:48:11.741 --> 01:48:12.992
Call yourself a brother? You're...

1535
01:48:13.076 --> 01:48:15.370
Look. come here... Mum. Okay. okay.

1536
01:48:17.497 --> 01:48:19.416
Every time.

1537
01:48:23.294 --> 01:48:24.295
Owen.

1538
01:48:24.671 --> 01:48:25.880
In position.

1539
01:48:27.424 --> 01:48:28.425
Go.

1540
01:48:30.010 --> 01:48:31.177
I'm in.

1541
01:48:31.720 --> 01:48:33.304
(PANTING)

1542
01:48:46.067 --> 01:48:47.444
(CELL PHONE VIBRATING)

1543
01:48:49.738 --> 01:48:50.905
DECKARD: <i>I've got the package. Toretto.</i>

1544
01:48:51.948 --> 01:48:53.616
All 12 pounds of him.

1545
01:48:53.992 --> 01:48:55.368
Ah.

1546
01:48:55.452 --> 01:48:58.788
Dada. Dada.

1547
01:49:10.467 --> 01:49:11.676
- (BULLET RICOCHETS)
- (BOTH GASP)

1548
01:49:14.471 --> 01:49:16.389
You made me miss my shot.

1549
01:49:16.473 --> 01:49:18.308
What you think you're doing?

1550
01:49:20.769 --> 01:49:22.145
Looking at you dead in the eye.

1551
01:49:23.355 --> 01:49:24.647
(BOTH GRUNTING)

1552
01:49:33.198 --> 01:49:34.532
(GAGGING)

1553
01:49:35.158 --> 01:49:36.159
(YELLING)

1554
01:49:41.664 --> 01:49:42.665
(YELLING)

1555
01:49:42.874 --> 01:49:43.917
- (GRUNTS)
- (NECK SNAPS)

1556
01:49:45.418 --> 01:49:47.337
That was for Elena.

1557
01:49:51.007 --> 01:49:52.008
Rhodes.

1558
01:49:52.175 --> 01:49:53.843
DOM: <i>He's no longer with us.</i>

1559
01:49:54.844 --> 01:49:56.429
<i>Rhodes picked the wrong target.</i>

1560
01:49:57.806 --> 01:50:01.601
Congratulations. Dom.
You just killed your son.

1561
01:50:01.685 --> 01:50:04.521
<i>You're wrong. I just saved him.</i>

1562
01:50:05.313 --> 01:50:07.524
<i>And you just took your foot
off the tiger's neck.</i>

1563
01:50:16.032 --> 01:50:18.868
All right. governor. it's gonna get noisy.

1564
01:50:20.036 --> 01:50:21.663
This is for your ears.

1565
01:50:24.374 --> 01:50:25.375
(BEEPS)

1566
01:50:25.542 --> 01:50:26.543
(MUSIC PLAYING OVER HEADPHONES)

1567
01:50:26.626 --> 01:50:27.627
Good?

1568
01:50:28.545 --> 01:50:29.546
(COOS)

1569
01:50:30.588 --> 01:50:31.673
Let's go.

1570
01:50:34.050 --> 01:50:37.220
No! Stop him!
Do not let him get off this plane!

1571
01:50:40.056 --> 01:50:41.599
LITTLE NOBODY: We got another problem.

1572
01:50:41.683 --> 01:50:43.393
That truck's got
enough missiles to take us all out.

1573
01:50:43.643 --> 01:50:44.769
Then don't give 'em a target.

1574
01:50:44.853 --> 01:50:47.150
Everybody. get in front of us.
line up. and we'll take the hit.

1575
01:50:47.230 --> 01:50:50.150
What? I need to switch cars right now!

1576
01:51:01.119 --> 01:51:02.120
(IN RUSSIAN)

1577
01:51:02.203 --> 01:51:03.538
Target acquired.

1578
01:51:06.458 --> 01:51:08.626
- Roman. here comes the bad part.
- What?

1579
01:51:11.963 --> 01:51:13.048
(BOTH GRUNTING)

1580
01:51:14.215 --> 01:51:15.300
(WHOOPS)

1581
01:51:15.383 --> 01:51:17.635
Hang in there. guys.
We're almost to the lock.

1582
01:51:17.719 --> 01:51:20.597
It's easy for you to say
when your ass ain't on fire.

1583
01:51:26.102 --> 01:51:29.773
All right. little man.
this might be a little scary.

1584
01:51:30.190 --> 01:51:31.608
but it's gonna be a lot of fun.

1585
01:51:34.110 --> 01:51:35.487
(BOTH GRUNTING)

1586
01:51:43.078 --> 01:51:44.082
How's the music. good?

1587
01:51:44.162 --> 01:51:45.163
Ah.

1588
01:51:48.291 --> 01:51:49.459
(ALL GROANING)

1589
01:51:57.717 --> 01:51:58.968
They're locking on.

1590
01:51:59.052 --> 01:52:00.512
Sorry. guys. I got no tricks left.

1591
01:52:00.595 --> 01:52:01.558
What do we do now?

1592
01:52:01.638 --> 01:52:03.098
TEJ: <i>We start prayin'!</i>

1593
01:52:25.662 --> 01:52:26.663
Hell. yeah!

1594
01:52:39.426 --> 01:52:40.677
There's Dom!

1595
01:52:44.556 --> 01:52:46.057
What. is this guy on our side now?

1596
01:52:46.141 --> 01:52:48.018
Who the hell cares? He just saved our ass!

1597
01:52:51.688 --> 01:52:53.565
Good to be riding with you again. man.

1598
01:53:01.364 --> 01:53:02.532
(CHUCKLES)

1599
01:53:06.953 --> 01:53:08.455
Toretto just cleared the way for them.

1600
01:53:08.538 --> 01:53:10.001
Someone. give me something!

1601
01:53:10.081 --> 01:53:11.124
Torpedoes are ready.

1602
01:53:11.207 --> 01:53:12.250
Then launch them!

1603
01:53:25.764 --> 01:53:26.765
Shit.

1604
01:53:30.518 --> 01:53:32.312
- Take the wheel!
- I ain't takin' shit!

1605
01:53:32.395 --> 01:53:33.813
Take the wheel!

1606
01:53:34.314 --> 01:53:35.315
Where you goin'?

1607
01:53:35.940 --> 01:53:36.983
(GROANS)

1608
01:53:37.067 --> 01:53:38.321
This is crazy!

1609
01:53:38.401 --> 01:53:39.611
HOBBS: Speed up!

1610
01:53:42.781 --> 01:53:44.327
- Left and back!
- What?

1611
01:53:44.407 --> 01:53:46.659
Turn the goddamn wheel
to the left really quickly!

1612
01:53:53.667 --> 01:53:54.834
Boom. baby!

1613
01:53:59.089 --> 01:54:01.091
(MEN GRUNTING)

1614
01:54:01.675 --> 01:54:02.759
Goin' for a ride.

1615
01:54:08.264 --> 01:54:09.265
Back in a sec.

1616
01:54:11.726 --> 01:54:15.021
(ALL GRUNTING)

1617
01:54:24.572 --> 01:54:25.949
- Where's that smile?
- Ah.

1618
01:54:26.032 --> 01:54:27.200
There it is.

1619
01:54:32.997 --> 01:54:34.165
You were gonna shoot a baby?

1620
01:54:35.458 --> 01:54:37.585
You sick bastard.

1621
01:54:38.545 --> 01:54:39.713
You're not gonna wanna see this.

1622
01:54:44.134 --> 01:54:45.510
(GRUNTING)

1623
01:54:50.640 --> 01:54:52.225
(SNIFFS)

1624
01:54:53.101 --> 01:54:54.144
Is that you or him?

1625
01:54:55.979 --> 01:54:57.022
(SNIFFS)

1626
01:54:57.105 --> 01:54:58.898
Him. Good.

1627
01:54:59.232 --> 01:55:00.525
The torpedoes missed.

1628
01:55:00.608 --> 01:55:02.360
They're gonna reach the lock
before the sub does.

1629
01:55:02.444 --> 01:55:03.653
The hell they are.

1630
01:55:06.406 --> 01:55:07.741
Get ready for this.

1631
01:55:28.011 --> 01:55:29.012
Oh. shit!

1632
01:55:29.095 --> 01:55:30.430
We're gonna need a bigger truck.

1633
01:55:34.142 --> 01:55:35.393
(LAUGHING)

1634
01:55:41.900 --> 01:55:43.568
It's right under us! Get out the way!

1635
01:55:46.279 --> 01:55:47.614
(GRUNTING)

1636
01:55:51.201 --> 01:55:52.202
(GRUNTING)

1637
01:55:55.830 --> 01:55:56.915
Get us out of here!

1638
01:55:57.082 --> 01:55:58.625
Why are you always yelling?

1639
01:56:02.587 --> 01:56:03.880
This bitch is crazy!

1640
01:56:03.963 --> 01:56:05.340
- Look out!
- (GASPS)

1641
01:56:06.424 --> 01:56:07.425
(YELLS)

1642
01:56:11.471 --> 01:56:12.555
That's not good.

1643
01:56:14.015 --> 01:56:15.558
That's not good.

1644
01:56:19.312 --> 01:56:21.231
Please tell me there's nothing
to worry about!

1645
01:56:21.314 --> 01:56:22.732
We got this.

1646
01:56:25.777 --> 01:56:26.778
(YELLS)

1647
01:56:29.406 --> 01:56:30.865
- (GRUNTS)
- (SIGHS)

1648
01:56:31.282 --> 01:56:32.283
(LAUGHS)

1649
01:56:33.952 --> 01:56:34.953
(PANTING)

1650
01:56:35.370 --> 01:56:36.621
That's my girl.

1651
01:56:43.169 --> 01:56:45.842
The sub's too close.
We ain't making it to the gate in time.

1652
01:56:45.922 --> 01:56:47.132
We're just going to let it get away?

1653
01:56:47.465 --> 01:56:48.925
Not if I know Dom.

1654
01:56:54.014 --> 01:56:55.306
You lose. Dom.

1655
01:56:55.390 --> 01:56:57.726
<i>I destroyed two of your teams.</i>

1656
01:56:57.976 --> 01:57:00.270
<i>I killed your red-headed boyfriend.</i>

1657
01:57:00.353 --> 01:57:03.481
And I put two killers
on your untraceable plane.

1658
01:57:04.649 --> 01:57:07.402
<i>You lost the minute
you interrupted my honeymoon.</i>

1659
01:57:08.278 --> 01:57:10.113
<i>Now guess who I'm coming for.</i>

1660
01:57:10.697 --> 01:57:12.699
Put a heatseeker on him now.

1661
01:57:14.701 --> 01:57:15.827
(SHOUTS) Now!

1662
01:57:21.166 --> 01:57:22.167
Fire!

1663
01:57:26.504 --> 01:57:28.757
That's a goddamn heatseeker coming at us!

1664
01:57:31.509 --> 01:57:33.887
Peel off! Head to the shore!

1665
01:57:38.016 --> 01:57:39.851
- (BEEPING)
- (ENGINE REVVING)

1666
01:57:40.060 --> 01:57:42.812
All right. Come and get it.

1667
01:58:00.747 --> 01:58:01.873
No. no. no.

1668
01:58:03.750 --> 01:58:05.877
Dive! Dive!

1669
01:58:06.503 --> 01:58:07.712
<i>This...</i>

1670
01:58:07.879 --> 01:58:09.547
This is for my son.

1671
01:58:22.811 --> 01:58:24.062
(GASPS)

1672
01:58:28.858 --> 01:58:29.859
Dom!

1673
01:58:40.412 --> 01:58:41.413
(GRUNTS)

1674
01:59:02.809 --> 01:59:03.852
(GRUNTS)

1675
01:59:25.415 --> 01:59:26.416
(DOOR OPENS)

1676
01:59:26.750 --> 01:59:28.126
- (GUNSHOTS)
- (MAN GROANS)

1677
01:59:32.547 --> 01:59:33.885
You're out of bullets. Deckard.

1678
01:59:33.965 --> 01:59:36.593
Not like I'm gonna need a gun
to take care of you.

1679
01:59:37.969 --> 01:59:39.471
How did you find me?

1680
01:59:41.556 --> 01:59:42.932
DOM: <i>You want to see the old Dom?</i>

1681
01:59:44.309 --> 01:59:45.518
- (BEEPING)
<i>- Watch.</i>

1682
01:59:48.605 --> 01:59:50.065
Resourceful.

1683
01:59:50.607 --> 01:59:52.776
You have a lot to answer for. Cipher.

1684
01:59:53.360 --> 01:59:55.195
What you've put my family through.

1685
01:59:55.612 --> 01:59:57.072
My mother.

1686
01:59:58.448 --> 02:00:00.825
I'm gonna make sure that never happens again.

1687
02:00:01.534 --> 02:00:02.619
To anyone.

1688
02:00:03.370 --> 02:00:05.709
There is only one flaw in your plan.

1689
02:00:05.789 --> 02:00:06.831
What's that?

1690
02:00:06.915 --> 02:00:09.209
Only one of us has a parachute.

1691
02:00:12.045 --> 02:00:13.254
(WIND WHOOSHING)

1692
02:00:18.134 --> 02:00:19.135
(GRUNTING)

1693
02:00:22.931 --> 02:00:23.932
(GRUNTS)

1694
02:00:30.146 --> 02:00:31.356
(COOING)

1695
02:00:31.815 --> 02:00:33.316
Told you this would be fun.

1696
02:00:37.153 --> 02:00:38.488
Time to land. boys.

1697
02:00:49.082 --> 02:00:50.667
You know I never left you. Letty.

1698
02:00:50.750 --> 02:00:52.002
I know.

1699
02:00:52.419 --> 02:00:54.671
And you know I never will.

1700
02:00:56.172 --> 02:00:57.549
I know.

1701
02:00:59.718 --> 02:01:00.927
(LAUGHS)

1702
02:01:01.636 --> 02:01:02.637
(PANTING)

1703
02:01:07.517 --> 02:01:09.394
I have so much to tell you.

1704
02:01:10.061 --> 02:01:14.065
Yeah. you do.
And you can start with that bitch.

1705
02:01:18.403 --> 02:01:21.698
Now. that's Dominic Toretto.

1706
02:01:23.783 --> 02:01:24.784
Hey. Dom!

1707
02:01:24.868 --> 02:01:28.959
I'm just throwin' it out there.
we need to get up outta here

1708
02:01:29.039 --> 02:01:32.295
'cause there's all kinda nuclearism
happening under this ice.

1709
02:01:32.375 --> 02:01:35.712
Relax. Without the trigger chips.
those nukes are harmless.

1710
02:01:36.087 --> 02:01:37.839
Okay. So we good. then.

1711
02:01:38.131 --> 02:01:41.051
Let me go on and get
my young selfie levels up.

1712
02:01:41.634 --> 02:01:43.553
You realize this is classified. right?

1713
02:01:43.636 --> 02:01:45.013
Not today.

1714
02:01:45.805 --> 02:01:46.890
(CAMERA CLICKS)

1715
02:01:47.140 --> 02:01:48.186
Unbelievable.

1716
02:01:48.266 --> 02:01:50.769
All right. can we get up
outta here. now? I'm freezin'!

1717
02:02:18.630 --> 02:02:19.798
It's okay.

1718
02:02:20.590 --> 02:02:22.717
Don't worry. He's gonna be here soon.

1719
02:02:23.093 --> 02:02:24.844
ROMAN: I get it. Y'all got a lot in common.

1720
02:02:24.928 --> 02:02:27.892
Computer hacks. God's Eye.
geeks. nerd... You know.

1721
02:02:27.972 --> 02:02:29.599
But we got a lot in common. too. right?

1722
02:02:29.683 --> 02:02:30.854
Like what?

1723
02:02:30.934 --> 02:02:34.312
We walk in the room
and we're oozin' sex appeal.

1724
02:02:34.396 --> 02:02:36.648
Me and you. hip to hip. is a problem.

1725
02:02:36.731 --> 02:02:39.150
I'm askin' a real question right now.

1726
02:02:39.234 --> 02:02:42.487
Is it gonna be <i>Revenge of the Nerds</i>

1727
02:02:43.279 --> 02:02:46.950
or <i>The Dark Knight?</i> Huh?

1728
02:02:47.283 --> 02:02:49.247
To be honest. I like both of you.

1729
02:02:49.327 --> 02:02:50.912
(ROMAN AND TEJ EXCLAIMING)

1730
02:02:52.414 --> 02:02:55.333
But just before we get into all of that.

1731
02:02:55.417 --> 02:02:57.210
let me ask you one question.

1732
02:02:57.293 --> 02:02:59.170
You can ask me anything.

1733
02:02:59.254 --> 02:03:00.380
Anything.

1734
02:03:00.463 --> 02:03:01.798
What's my last name?

1735
02:03:04.676 --> 02:03:08.099
When you guys figure it out.
then. I guess you can let me know.

1736
02:03:08.179 --> 02:03:10.849
It's gonna be Parker.
That's all that really matters.

1737
02:03:10.932 --> 02:03:12.267
- ROMAN: Jones.
- TEJ: Mrs. Parker.

1738
02:03:12.684 --> 02:03:14.644
- Right?
- Hey. Mrs. Parker...

1739
02:03:15.186 --> 02:03:16.187
LETTY: Hey.

1740
02:03:16.271 --> 02:03:17.564
Letty.

1741
02:03:17.647 --> 02:03:19.149
I wanted to thank you.

1742
02:03:19.691 --> 02:03:20.692
No need.

1743
02:03:21.943 --> 02:03:22.944
Well...

1744
02:03:23.278 --> 02:03:25.951
Cipher's still on the loose.
There's been some reports she's in Athens.

1745
02:03:26.031 --> 02:03:28.453
but she won't be nuking
any cities anytime soon.

1746
02:03:28.533 --> 02:03:29.743
Thanks to you guys.

1747
02:03:29.826 --> 02:03:31.915
So. I got you a party favor.

1748
02:03:31.995 --> 02:03:33.580
- (MR. NOBODY LAUGHS)
- HOBBS: This can't be good.

1749
02:03:33.663 --> 02:03:36.166
Your record's been cleared.
Full reinstatement.

1750
02:03:36.249 --> 02:03:37.796
You've got your job back.

1751
02:03:37.876 --> 02:03:39.377
That is. if you want it.

1752
02:03:42.797 --> 02:03:43.927
If I want?

1753
02:03:44.007 --> 02:03:45.008
Mmm-hmm.

1754
02:03:45.091 --> 02:03:46.676
(LAUGHS)

1755
02:03:51.514 --> 02:03:55.685
You know. after 16 years.
I figure it's time for a little break.

1756
02:03:56.311 --> 02:03:57.479
Wow.

1757
02:03:59.064 --> 02:04:01.024
Daddy's stayin' home.

1758
02:04:02.442 --> 02:04:03.693
(LAUGHS)

1759
02:04:07.530 --> 02:04:08.573
Nobody.

1760
02:04:08.656 --> 02:04:09.699
Keep in touch.

1761
02:04:10.158 --> 02:04:11.743
Ah. Hang on a second.

1762
02:04:12.077 --> 02:04:14.245
This could be interesting.

1763
02:04:19.167 --> 02:04:20.335
(SIGHS) What made you think I'd do it?

1764
02:04:21.544 --> 02:04:22.799
Brotherhood.

1765
02:04:22.879 --> 02:04:26.508
I saw that look you gave Cipher.
knew you wanted revenge.

1766
02:04:26.841 --> 02:04:28.343
Glad I did it.

1767
02:04:31.680 --> 02:04:34.182
I can't believe you went to see my mother.

1768
02:04:35.225 --> 02:04:37.435
(BOTH CHUCKLE)

1769
02:04:49.489 --> 02:04:51.491
All this fuss over you.

1770
02:04:52.158 --> 02:04:53.451
(COOING)

1771
02:04:57.497 --> 02:04:58.915
Yes.

1772
02:05:04.004 --> 02:05:07.090
Elena. I promised to keep our son safe.

1773
02:05:09.259 --> 02:05:11.428
And now. he always will be.

1774
02:05:19.561 --> 02:05:23.857
I wanna introduce you to the most
important person in my universe.

1775
02:05:25.525 --> 02:05:27.944
One who never gave up on me.

1776
02:05:33.616 --> 02:05:34.701
He's beautiful.

1777
02:05:36.453 --> 02:05:40.790
DOM: You've heard me say that you
never turn your back on family.

1778
02:05:42.751 --> 02:05:46.796
and I wanna thank you all
for never turning your back on me.

1779
02:05:51.384 --> 02:05:52.969
You wanna meet them?

1780
02:05:53.636 --> 02:05:55.138
All right.

1781
02:05:55.972 --> 02:05:57.307
Everyone.

1782
02:05:58.641 --> 02:06:00.060
meet Brian.

1783
02:06:01.144 --> 02:06:02.979
(LAUGHTER. APPLAUSE)

1784
02:06:05.940 --> 02:06:06.941
(COOING)

1785
02:06:09.319 --> 02:06:10.570
HOBBS: To Brian!

1786
02:06:10.653 --> 02:06:12.530
ROMAN: Welcome to the family. Brian.

1787
02:06:12.614 --> 02:06:15.325
Okay. I guess it's my turn to say grace.

1788
02:06:15.784 --> 02:06:18.290
We thank you for giving us family.

1789
02:06:18.370 --> 02:06:22.749
We sit here in praise.
Thank you for giving us the strength...

